WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.250
- As I have for every movie
in the "Chucky" franchise,

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.990
I'm gonna go over everything
you might've missed

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.340
in season one of "Chucky".

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.990
With eight episodes,
there's a lot to cover.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.040
So let's start at the beginning

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.420
with the opening title sequence.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.280
Each episode has a unique title animation

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.510
that plays over the theme song.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.340
And this theme song may sound familiar,

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.260
because it's actually a
re-orchestrated version

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.810
of a track from the original
score for "Child's Play 2".

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.340
Let me play them both for comparison.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.969
Here's the theme from the show.

00:00:21.969 --> 00:00:24.719
(sinister music)

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.420
And here's a clip from "Child's Play 2".

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.470
I'll take out the dialogue

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.348
so you can just focus on the music.

00:00:30.348 --> 00:00:33.515
(slow sinister music)

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.500
Choosing a track from "Child's Play 2"

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.030
lets the viewer know that this season

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.560
is a tribute to that second movie.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.780
The season features more
elements of "Child's Play 2"

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.420
than we've seen since,
well, "Child's Play 2".

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.440
Just as "Curse of Chucky"

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.577
was a sort of second coming
of the first "Child's Play",

00:00:48.577 --> 00:00:50.910
"Chucky" season one would
be a sort of second coming

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:51.743
of its sequel.

00:00:51.743 --> 00:00:53.347
Not only is the story very similar,

00:00:53.347 --> 00:00:55.590
"Child's Play 2" is about
Andy going to a foster home

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:56.670
where he's hunted by Chucky

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.770
and "Chucky" season one
is about Jake Wheeler

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.510
receiving foster care
from his aunt and uncle

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.190
after his dad is electrocuted by Chucky,

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.510
but the visual design of the show

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.000
also calls back to that 1990 sequel.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.970
- Chucky's look, we've
taken a lot of pains

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:11.940
to mimic the specific
look of the doll himself

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:12.910
from "Child's Play 2".

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:14.587
I was just talking to someone who said,

00:01:14.587 --> 00:01:17.550
"It's the creepiest version,
but weirdly also the cutest."

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.710
- [Zac] In this feature,
series creator Don Mancini

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.450
explains why he chose the second movie

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.190
as an inspiration for the series.

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.020
- I've heard over the years from fans

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.960
telling me that "Child's
Play 2" is their favorite.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:31.290
Now, with the TV series, it
was the perfect opportunity

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:35.430
to dig into where those
characters are now 30 years on.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:37.500
- This was the first time
we got to see Andy and Kyle

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.580
work together since then.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.590
And the show even uses
their original actors,

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:42.630
Alex Vincent and Christine Elise.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.450
Kyle even brings back her
signature hatch from that movie.

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.340
There are many, many more parallels

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.840
and Easter eggs I can point out.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.040
So let's go through the series

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.930
and explore all of its secrets.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:52.800
To learn about the meaning

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.480
behind the advertisements at the school,

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.090
how Halloween decorations
foreshadow specific deaths,

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:58.710
who this realtor really is,

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:01.170
the significance of every
name on these tombstones,

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.520
and so much more.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.780
Stick around to the end of this video.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:07.613
(dark rock music)

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.810
Welcome to "Things You Missed".

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:14.970
They say you can't keep a good guy down.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.890
A lot of times when a
series gets a reboot,

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.410
fans have to say goodbye
to any hopes of revisiting

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.610
the original continuity.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.320
The Chucky franchise got that reboot

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.970
with "Child's Play" in 2019,

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:25.830
but the original voodoo-powered Chucky

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.690
was not ready to give up the spotlight.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:29.760
Don Mancini, who has
been with this franchise

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.890
since the beginning, had
been doing some work in TV

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:32.940
on the show "Hannibal"

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:35.610
and was inspired to try "Chucky"
as a weekly show as well.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:37.380
Now, instead of an 80-minute movie,

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.480
we have a six-hour season to analyze,

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:40.500
which means there's more room

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.360
for a ton of things you missed.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:43.531
Let's get into them.

00:02:43.531 --> 00:02:44.912
(sword scrapes)

00:02:44.912 --> 00:02:47.662
(sinister music)

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.490
The series opens with this POV shot

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:51.630
of the young Charles Lee Ray

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.030
going upstairs and seeing his
mother combining your hair.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.680
This is the first of many homages

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.030
to the "Halloween" franchise.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.860
The original "Halloween" opens with a POV

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:00.570
of the young Michael Myers going upstairs

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:02.010
and seeing his sister combining her hair

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:03.420
in the exact same fashion.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.857
We've seen "Chucky" films steal
"Halloween" openings before.

00:03:05.857 --> 00:03:08.100
"Seed of Chucky" has pretty
much the same opening

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.470
and "Cult of Chucky" has a
psychiatric patient transfer

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.840
at the beginning, much like
several "Halloween" movies.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.700
So there are always a lot
of "Halloween" references

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:15.533
in Chucky movies.

00:03:15.533 --> 00:03:16.560
Just because Michael Myers

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.990
is like a supernatural
slasher forefather to Chucky.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.940
But this time, there
are even more than usual

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.190
because the series takes
place around Halloween.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:25.110
By the way, can you guess
the only other Chucky film

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:26.370
to take place in October?

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.660
It's "Child's Play 2".

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:28.710
Another "Halloween" reference

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:30.960
is the inclusion of a
character named Dr. Mixter.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.300
This brings to mind the
doctor from "Halloween II".

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.160
- [Woman] Try to relax, Laurie.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.380
Dr. Mixter will have you
stitched up in no time.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:38.460
- I'm sure it's no mistake

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.170
that when we first hear Dr. Mixter's name

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.220
brought up by Lexy's mom,

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.950
she's actually speaking
about Halloween, the holiday.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.480
- Besides Dr. Mixter says

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.340
that Halloween is the perfect opportunity

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:48.690
for you girls to bond.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:50.310
- By the way, this is not the first time

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:51.510
that we've seen a Chucky character

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:53.100
named after a Halloween character.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.170
In "Child's Play 3", we
met Colonel Cochrane,

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:57.750
who was named after Colonel
Cochrane from "Halloween III".

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.040
I may have neglected to mention that

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.360
in my "Child's Play 3" video.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.310
Another parallel can
be seen in episode two,

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:05.190
where we see a flashback
to Charles Lee Ray in 1965

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:07.080
where he dresses up as
a clown for Halloween.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.100
In the movie "Halloween",

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.960
Michael Myers also dresses up as a clown

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.090
for a Halloween night in the 1960s.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.400
In that same scene, we see
Charles bite into an apple

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.390
with a razor in it.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.340
A kid in "Halloween II"
does the same thing.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:18.900
I'll note that this
might not be a reference

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:19.860
to the "Halloween II" kid.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.450
It could just be about the urban legend

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.190
that the "Halloween II" kid is based on.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:25.170
It's the same thing with
Lexy and her sister.

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:26.640
Lexy has plans on Halloween night,

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.290
but her parents tell her
that they're going out

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.570
so she has to babysit
Caroline and she's annoyed.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.500
I found myself wondering

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.540
if this is supposed to be a
reference to "Halloween 4",

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.370
where Rachel Carruthers
is forced to babysit

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.600
her adoptive sister Jamie

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.250
while her parents go
out on Halloween night,

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.140
thus ruining her plans for the evening.

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:41.820
There might be another
"Halloween" connection

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:43.680
involving Lexy and her
sister the next night

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:45.180
when she's putting Caroline down to bed

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.348
and Caroline asks her to sing a lullaby.

00:04:47.348 --> 00:04:48.893
- Bedtime. You have to sing to me.

00:04:48.893 --> 00:04:50.730
- So Lexy sings "Don't Fear the Reaper"

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:51.780
by Blue Oyster Cult,

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.640
the same song that Laurie
and Annie listened to

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.140
in the car in "Halloween 1".

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.550
And as much as I like the song,

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:59.280
I'm getting pretty tired of
hearing it in movies and TV.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.807
We already heard it in
"Halloween", "Zombieland",

00:05:01.807 --> 00:05:03.240
"Gone Girl", and "Scream".

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.650
And that's just covering the movies

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:06.330
that I analyzed here
on "Things You Missed".

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:09.090
Forget the other 76 productions
that it's been in so far,

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:10.350
according to IMDB.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:11.790
In the flashback where we see the death

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.020
of Charles Lee Ray's parents,

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:15.090
his mom tries to hide him
in a shuttered closet,

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:16.680
just like the one that
Laurie Strode hides in

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:17.513
in "Halloween".

00:05:17.513 --> 00:05:18.510
And in episode four,

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.910
Chucky terrorizes the
Hackensack Memorial Hospital,

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:22.890
which is abbreviated to HMH,

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:24.630
just like the Haddonfield
Memorial Hospital

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:26.670
from "Halloween II" and "Halloween Kills".

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:29.340
Later on, "Halloween's" final
girl comes up in a discussion

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.590
between Devon and Jake
about horror movies.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:32.640
- Favorite final girl?

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.260
- Laurie Strode hands down.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:35.820
- Jamie Lee's gonna win
the Saturn this year.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:37.050
- Dude, she's gonna win an Oscar.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.190
She's magnificent.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:41.100
- Spoiler alert: Jamie Lee
Curtis did not win an Oscar

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:42.120
for "Halloween Kills".

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:43.380
At the time of recording this video,

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.600
the Saturn Awards have
not yet taken place.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.010
Shortly after this conversation,

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:49.170
Chucky breaks into the
house and kills the lights,

00:05:49.170 --> 00:05:51.210
something that Michael
Myers is known for doing.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:52.620
And finally, we have Andy and Kyle

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.960
stopping at an auto
repair shop/gas station

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.820
and Andy strands her
there for her own good.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:58.350
Michael Myers strands Dr. Loomis

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:00.810
at an auto repair/gas
station in "Halloween 4".

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:02.940
And that is not the end of this video.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.920
That's just the end of the
"Halloween" references.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.600
So let's get back to the
beginning of the series

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:08.640
when Jake is first buying
Chucky at the yard sale.

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:10.350
According to this video with Don Mancini,

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:12.360
this is actually Tiffany
crossing through right here.

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:14.010
She wears this red coat
later in the season

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:16.080
so she's probably checking in
to make sure that an innocent,

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.970
like Jake, is the one who
ends up with the doll.

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:19.560
When Jake walks home from the yard sale,

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.660
there are a couple more
Easter eggs on the podcast

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.127
that he's listening to.

00:06:23.127 --> 00:06:25.400
(sinister music)

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.144
(thunder rumbles)

00:06:28.144 --> 00:06:31.860
(sinister electronic music)

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:34.380
Jake is listening to Devon's
podcast "Hackenslash",

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:35.610
which, according to this graphic,

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:37.440
posts new episodes every Tuesday.

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:40.290
The "Chucky" series also release
new episodes on Tuesdays.

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:42.427
We can see that Jake is
currently on episode eight.

00:06:42.427 --> 00:06:44.940
"Chucky" season one is
an eight episode season.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:47.040
As Devon explains the morbid
history of Hackensack,

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:48.180
we see graphics on screen

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:49.530
that go along with what he's saying.

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:51.420
This one, which appears
for just one moment,

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:53.340
is the same article on
the Lakeshore Strangler

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.500
that Tiffany kept in her
trailer in "Bride of Chucky".

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.360
Shortly after that,
there's another article

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.000
which appears to be from a
website written by Ethan Carson.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.890
This article appears
again in episode seven

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:02.940
on Devon's corkboard.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.770
This is our first crew
reference Easter egg.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.990
Ethan Carson is the art
department assistant.

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:09.720
Then after 56 seconds, the podcast ends.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:10.950
That was a short podcast.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.720
Jake goes home and we see his room.

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:15.030
He's got a poster for a
band called Mad Ashes.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.920
This might be a clue of things to come.

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:19.140
Later on, we see Chucky
return with a vengeance

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:20.250
after surviving a fire.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.050
And similarly, we see Andy's wrath

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:23.730
after escaping from an explosion.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:26.060
We also meet Jake's cat, Banksy.

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:26.893
- Banskys.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.270
Here, Banks.

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:32.130
- Banksy is an artist known
for his street murals,

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:34.050
but he's also worked
in many other mediums,

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.850
like Jake's forte sculpting.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.460
When Banksy bites the dust,
so does Jake's sculpture.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:40.410
The next day, Jake brings Chucky to school

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:41.730
and he's picked on by a classmate

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:43.290
named Oliver Hayden on the bus.

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.450
Oliver throws a pair of
gym shorts in his face.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.010
That's a pretty hostile thing to do

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.620
and it reminds me a lot of
the extremely hostile kid

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.240
on the bus in "Child's Play 2",

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.470
which, if you watch my channel,

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.990
you know I always, always,
always have to bring up.

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.310
Why are you so hostile?

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:57.630
Oliver is also wearing yellow,

00:07:57.630 --> 00:07:59.760
so he matches the kid that
was throwing stuff on the bus

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:00.870
in "Child's Play 2".

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:03.480
Just because this season is
themed around the second film,

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.940
that doesn't mean that each of
the others isn't referenced.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:07.170
In the cafeteria at school,

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.180
there's an advertisement
for a hearty bowl of chili,

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:10.890
the same meal that the Pierce family eats

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:13.170
in the famous chili scene
from "Curse of Chucky".

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:14.910
- I love chili.

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:15.810
- This is amazing.

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:17.580
- I can't believe there's no meat in this.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:19.350
And it's so hearty.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.760
- Speaking of not having meats,

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:23.370
the banner also advertises
a beyond meat burger.

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:25.740
That might be the scariest
thing of this whole episode.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:27.900
The drinks being served
are a bright red punch,

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.280
'cause there's gonna be blood.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:31.320
When Devon sits by Jake and
asks what he's watching.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:33.360
Jake says that he's watching
"The Vampire Diaries".

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:34.980
Now I haven't seen "The Vampire Diaries",

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:37.080
but this Reddit post from cesardaniel02

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.730
talks about how there
are a lot of similarities

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:39.750
between the two series.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:41.430
Both are part of this teen horror genre

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:43.050
with an expanding network of villains.

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:45.150
Vampires can turn people
into fellow vampires

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:45.983
to grow their ranks,

00:08:45.983 --> 00:08:48.990
and Chucky can possess dolls
or people to grow his ranks.

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:50.550
The post also talks about similarities

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:52.620
between the characters
like Jake and Jeremy,

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:54.330
such as how both lose their parents.

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:55.710
I'll link the post in the description

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:56.850
if you want to read further.

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:58.620
After receiving a call from Andy Barclay,

00:08:58.620 --> 00:08:59.700
warning him about Chucky,

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:01.560
Jake looks up Good Guy Doll violence

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:03.390
on a search engine called Search.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:05.130
If you've been keeping up
with my Chucky episodes,

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:07.170
then you're already familiar
with the strange handling

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:09.150
of website brand names
in the world of Chucky.

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:11.070
For example, Curse is careful to specify

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:13.560
that Nica uses "Internet
Search" instead of Google.

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:16.560
But one movie later, in
Cult, Andy namedrops Google.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:18.720
The series has similar inconsistencies.

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.610
Chucky stalks Lexy on a social media site

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:21.690
called SquarePix,

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:24.177
but later on specifically uses the words--

00:09:24.177 --> 00:09:26.760
- Instagram influencers.

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:27.660
- There's even a joke

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:30.000
where the kids try to find
Andy Barclay on social media

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.710
by searching Insta, Snap, and Twitter

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.930
and then Devon eventually
finds him on Facebook

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:34.763
and he's laughing

00:09:34.763 --> 00:09:36.570
'cause of course the old
person would be on Facebook.

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:37.920
They should've checked there first.

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:40.260
- [Devon] Hey, Lexy. He's on Facebook.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.330
- Anyway, as Jake is looking
into the Chucky dolls

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.880
passed on Search, each of the
results references an incident

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:46.200
from a previous Chucky movie.

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:47.820
The first four are from "Child's Play".

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:50.550
The headlines read, "six-year-old
boy says Chucky did it,"

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:53.280
which is Andy, "Urban legends:
Charles Lee Ray and Chucky,

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.230
Boy's Babysitter Dies in Freak Accident,"

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:56.130
which is Aunt Maggie,

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:58.320
and "Explosion on South
Side Leaves One Dead,"

00:09:58.320 --> 00:09:59.686
which is Eddie Caputo.

00:09:59.686 --> 00:10:01.740
(gun fires)
(house explodes)

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:03.690
The next one is about the
teacher from "Child's Play 2"

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:05.340
and we get a new piece of information.

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:07.860
We've always known that Andy's
teacher was Miss Kettlewell,

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:10.740
but for the first time they
reveal her first name Elizabeth.

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.930
The last results talks
about the Play Pal CEO

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:15.060
from "Child's Play 2"
and "3", Mr. Sullivan.

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:17.460
And we learned his first
name as well Haskell.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:18.293
You hear that?

00:10:18.293 --> 00:10:20.130
That's the sound of
Wiki pages being updated

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:21.150
across the internet.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:22.890
Jake confirms that his doll is alive,

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:24.900
the same way that Karen
Barclay did in the first movie:

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:25.830
by discovering that he's been

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:27.150
able to talk without batteries.

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:29.340
His response is to throw
Chucky in the trash.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:30.210
What the hell is that gonna do

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:31.530
when you already know he's alive?

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:32.580
I think this shot is here

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:34.440
more for the sake of keeping
up with the tradition

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.270
of characters throwing
Chucky in the trash.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:38.940
Kyle does it in 2, Colonel
Cochrane does it in 3,

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:41.250
Sarah does it in Curse,
Claire does it in Cult,

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:43.530
Andy does it in the
remake, and in episode five

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:46.080
Lexy's dad also attempts to
throw Chucky in the trash.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.150
Obviously Jake trashing
his doll doesn't work

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:50.820
and he appears shortly thereafter
at the school talent show.

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:53.400
- I see some familiar
faces in the crowd tonight.

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:55.770
- [Zac] From this line, we cut
to a shot of Lexy's family.

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:57.840
And indeed, there is
a familiar face there,

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:59.460
because her father is played by an actor

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:01.950
named Michael Therriault,
who also played Dr. Foley

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:03.990
in the previous installment
"Cult of Chucky".

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:05.910
The split screen editing
technique in this scene

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:07.770
is also something that
was taken from Cult.

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.480
Speaking of familiar faces,

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:11.250
there are a lot of repeats in the crowd.

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.560
A lot of doppelgangers
in Hackensack, I guess.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:14.850
They might have been low on extras

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:16.950
or maybe this was some
kind of COVID precaution.

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:19.020
Chucky makes it appear
as if Jake is performing

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:20.550
a ventriloquist act on stage.

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:21.870
This is the same trick used by Glen

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:23.310
at the beginning of "Seed of Chucky".

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:25.110
That night, the power goes out in a storm

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:27.510
and Jake's dad goes to the
basement to use the breaker box.

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:29.730
We're shown to this shot of a
spider web in the foreground.

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:31.560
It's the first shot we
see of Jake's basement

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.570
and it's just like the first
shot we see of the attic

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:35.310
in "Curse of Chucky" and "Seed of Chucky",

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:37.530
both of which also have us
looking through a spider web.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:38.490
The first episode ends

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:40.320
with the first onscreen
kill of the series,

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:42.870
which is Jake's dad, Lucas
Wheeler getting electrocuted.

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:44.550
Remember how I said this
series has an emphasis

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:45.420
on "Child's Play 2"?

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:47.610
Well, an electrocution
is also the first death

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:48.443
in that movie.

00:11:48.443 --> 00:11:49.530
Because he's now an orphan,

00:11:49.530 --> 00:11:51.540
Jake would be moved into
his aunt and uncle's house,

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:54.120
which contains many
more things you missed.

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:58.486
- And now a word from our sponsors.

00:11:58.486 --> 00:12:01.236
(sinister music)

00:12:02.828 --> 00:12:05.495
(ominous music)

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:08.760
- When Jake Wheeler finally
has a moment to himself again,

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:11.130
he has a lot of questions
for his retro doll.

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:12.690
- Talk to me.

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:13.950
I said talk to me, damn it!

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:15.930
- It's almost the same
line that Andy's mom

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:18.150
confronted the Chucky doll
with in "Child's Play".

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:19.860
- Say something, damn it!

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:22.080
- We next see Jake a
week later on Halloween.

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:23.910
He and his cousin, Junior,
get home from school

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:26.190
and Junior's having some trouble
with the security system.

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:28.080
It turns out that Junior's
dad changed the code

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.220
and Jake lets him know.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.380
Junior is essentially
no longer the only child

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:33.270
and he feels a sense
of jealousy as a result

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:35.070
and this fuels the rivalry between them.

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:36.240
The tension between the two boys

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:37.350
builds throughout the episode

00:12:37.350 --> 00:12:39.570
and it eventually leads
to Mr. and Mrs. Wheeler

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:41.700
sitting down to discuss if
it's actually a good idea

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:42.660
to look after Jake.

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:43.770
Can we just pause it here?

00:12:43.770 --> 00:12:45.300
If you're a parent, take note,

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:48.450
this is a terrible place to
have a secret conversation.

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:51.390
- He's not a violent kid.
He's just traumatized.

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:52.650
- We're all traumatized.

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:55.560
I mean, are we even qualified
to look after a boy like this?

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:57.180
- [Zac] This is the exact same situation

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:58.950
that Andy's caretakers found themselves in

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:01.260
after taking him in in "Child's Play 2".

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:04.350
- Are we even qualified to
take care of a boy like this?

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:06.120
- And they later have
a conversation about it

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:08.070
that is also eavesdropped upon.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:11.160
- You have to admit, he's
a very troubled little boy.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:12.810
I mean, obviously he's not come to terms

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.610
with this whole doll thing.

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:16.290
- Going forward, the
Wheeler house would become

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:17.790
the main location in the series.

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:19.320
It would be the stage for three deaths

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:20.610
and one additional funeral.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.530
And the cherry blossom
designs all over the walls

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:23.670
serve as a symbol for this.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:25.320
They almost look like splatters of blood

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:26.460
sprayed upon the walls.

00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:28.500
It's also fitting that
they have four skeletons

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:29.580
on display for Halloween,

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:31.260
representing the four
members of the family

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:32.370
who would die this season.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:34.960
Bree, Logan, and Junior,
and the maid Annie.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.780
- Annie really was a part of this family.

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:39.060
- [Zac] The ones in the middle
are a couple, Bree and Logan,

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:41.070
which are the middle two
deaths chronologically.

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:42.750
Jake confronts Chucky about Annie's death,

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:44.610
but Chucky denies the allegation.

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:48.150
- Swear to God, I didn't kill her.

00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:49.590
- However, if you've seen Curse,

00:13:49.590 --> 00:13:51.960
you know that swearing to
God means nothing to Chucky.

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:53.970
- There is no God.

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:55.410
- [Zac] Chucky tries to convince Jake

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:56.610
with an offer of friendship.

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:59.320
- I'm your friend to the end.

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:01.203
- F*ck with that sh*t.

00:14:01.203 --> 00:14:02.036
I'm not six years old.

00:14:02.036 --> 00:14:03.510
- That's a reference to "Child's Play" one

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:05.730
which takes place on
Andy's sixth birthday.

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:08.070
- We're friends to the end, remember?

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:09.990
- Chucky's manipulation tactics continue

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:12.690
as he tries to relate to
Jake using his sexuality.

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:15.510
- You know, I have a queer kid.

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:16.740
- You have a kid?

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:18.960
- Chucky seems to be talking
about Glen and Glenda

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:19.920
from "Seed of Chucky".

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:21.000
If you haven't seen Seed,

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.520
it's about Chucky and Tiffany's
child who is born as a doll

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:25.260
and thus has no private parts.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.750
So Chucky and Tiffany argue
about if it's a boy or a girl

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:29.850
causing the kid to switch
between the two identities,

00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:30.720
Glen and Glenda.

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:32.790
We haven't seen Glen or Glenda since then,

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:35.010
but I'm guessing switching
between the two alter egos

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:36.900
may have caused the
grown up Glen and Glenda

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:38.370
to be considered by bisexual,

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:40.470
which is probably what
Chucky is referencing here.

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:43.380
Glenda actually gets a second
reference in episode eight.

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:44.760
- [Junior] What's that?

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:46.560
- Isn't it cute?

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:49.260
My darling Glenda gave it to me.

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:51.780
They have exquisite taste.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.520
- [Zac] Meanwhile, over at Lexy's house,

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:55.500
Caroline has developed
an obsession with Chucky

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:57.480
ever since seeing him
insult her older sister

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:58.440
at the talent show.

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:00.810
There's no way in hell a little
kid could draw this well,

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:02.550
but the whole thing reminds me of Madeline

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:05.010
from "Cult of Chucky", who also
became attached to the doll

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:06.900
and started sketching pictures of him.

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:09.060
- [Mr. Cross] Baby, can
you remember his name?

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:10.390
- [Caroline] Chucky.

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:11.610
- (chuckles) Yes, that's right.

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:13.530
- That might be the
dumbest thing I've heard.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:15.240
You think she can remember and reproduce

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:16.620
every little detail about him,

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:18.300
including the text on his pocket

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:20.370
yet she wouldn't be able
to remember his name?

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:21.570
What the hell is wrong with you?

00:15:21.570 --> 00:15:22.590
Why would you ask that?

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:23.940
Can you remember his name?

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:25.890
That evening, Devon's mom breaks the news

00:15:25.890 --> 00:15:27.210
about what happened to Annie.

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:28.530
Devon is a true crime buff

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:30.180
and his room is decorated
with news clippings

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:31.230
about famous criminals.

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:33.960
He seems to have a particular
interest in the Zodiac case.

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:35.700
I covered "Zodiac" here
on Things You Missed

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.470
and one of the things I
mentioned in that movie

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:39.630
was how they used real
newspaper clippings in the film

00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:41.730
to make everything look
as authentic as possible.

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:43.920
Perhaps as an homage,
the same is done here.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:46.140
Some of the other true crime
cases that he has on display

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:47.610
are real articles as well.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:49.260
Despite Annie's untimely death,

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.960
Junior still decides to go over
to Oliver's Halloween party.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:53.790
When his ride pulls up,
there's a cameo appearance

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:55.830
from Don Mancini as the Uber driver.

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:58.590
It's hard to tell if it's him,
but he confirmed on Twitter.

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:00.570
When we arrive on the
scene of Oliver's party,

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:02.490
it's gotta be the most
lit middle school party

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:03.690
in the history of the world.

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:04.620
When I was in middle school,

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:06.090
I don't remember any of my classmates

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:07.410
pulling up in a Maserati.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:08.310
I mean, I've been to parties

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:10.140
thrown by some of the biggest YouTubers

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:12.000
and even those are not on this level.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.140
Except for my party.

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:15.028
My party was the greatest.

00:16:15.028 --> 00:16:16.037
(metal music)

00:16:16.037 --> 00:16:16.870
♪ Ahem. ♪

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:19.022
♪ EVERYBODY'S OUT TO GET ME! ♪

00:16:19.022 --> 00:16:21.160
- [Wavywebsurf] Oh my, what the f--

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:22.770
- There are at least
three kids at this party

00:16:22.770 --> 00:16:24.000
dressed up in army gear.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.220
The third movie takes place
at a military academy.

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:27.210
Away from the action,

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:29.070
Chucky and Caroline have
already made friends

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:31.050
and Chucky has already
begun to try to convince her

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:32.103
to kill her sister.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:36.240
- Mommy says real killing is bad.

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:38.670
- Yeah, well mommy's full of sh**.

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:41.093
- Mommy says it isn't nice to swear.

00:16:41.093 --> 00:16:45.690
- Mommy's working her way up
my list pretty ****ing quick.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:46.980
- If you're keeping counts at home,

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:49.170
this is now the third
child that has taken issue

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:51.510
with Chucky's colorful vocabulary.

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:53.757
- Charles, stop swearing.

00:16:53.757 --> 00:16:55.500
- Chucky, stop cursing.

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:56.333
- We actually see

00:16:56.333 --> 00:16:58.710
that Chucky first began
teaching profanity to children

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:01.080
as a 14-year-old when he was
staying at the foster home

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:02.460
for wayward boys.

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:03.874
- How was the story, boys?

00:17:03.874 --> 00:17:04.980
- ****ing Fantastic.

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:06.600
- Language, young man.

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:07.860
Where did you learn that?

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.660
- When Jake realizes
that Chucky is missing,

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:10.740
he rushes to the party.

00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:12.330
But before he finds what he's looking for,

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.520
the crowd throws him
into a closet with Devon.

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:16.080
There's a false scare
with the little mannequin

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:17.100
wearing a hockey mask,

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:19.440
maybe a reference to Jason
from "Friday the 13th".

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:21.060
Before he's able to find Chucky,

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:23.340
Jake comes across this horrific scene

00:17:23.340 --> 00:17:25.560
where Lexy impersonates
his father's death.

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.960
I don't really know how she
figured out all of these details

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:29.160
about what he was wearing,

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:31.620
how he died and exactly
what it all looked like

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:33.120
when Mr. Wheeler met his fate

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:35.250
since the only one there
to witness Lucas's death,

00:17:35.250 --> 00:17:37.290
other than Jake, was Chucky himself.

00:17:37.290 --> 00:17:39.570
But in the next episode,
the creators of the show

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:42.330
would include a ton of jabs
at one Disney franchise

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:43.890
that has been in a long rivalry

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:45.895
with "Child's Play" and "Chucky".

00:17:45.895 --> 00:17:47.424
(sinister music)

00:17:47.424 --> 00:17:50.768
(thunder claps)

00:17:50.768 --> 00:17:53.193
(sinister music)

00:17:53.193 --> 00:17:54.540
(thunder rumbles)

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:55.530
By the third episode,

00:17:55.530 --> 00:17:57.480
Chucky has convinced Jake to kill Lexy.

00:17:57.480 --> 00:18:00.270
Well, I guess Lexy did most
of the convincing herself.

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:02.100
He tracks her phone and plans to jump her

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.690
while she's jogging in
the middle of the woods.

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:04.980
But it turns out to be Junior,

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:06.150
who had grabbed Lexy's phone

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:07.740
and apparently went on a run with it

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:09.870
instead of just giving
it back to her first.

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:10.830
- Hey, babe.

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:11.880
Oh, thanks for grabbing it.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:14.430
- And also, they are conveniently
wearing matching hoodies.

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:16.560
This is all clearly done
just to trick the audience,

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:17.670
which I'm never a fan of.

00:18:17.670 --> 00:18:20.010
However, the matching
outfits do act as a barometer

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:21.540
for their relationship going forward.

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:23.250
At this point early in the third episode,

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:24.780
Junior and Lexy are really close

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:26.070
because they're both kind of united

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:27.420
in their disdain of Jake.

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:28.710
But at the end of the episode,

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:31.350
Lexy learns that Chucky is
alive and trying to kill her.

00:18:31.350 --> 00:18:33.360
So she's forced a team
up with Jake and Devon,

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:35.400
causing her and Junior to drift apart.

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:37.980
By episode six, Junior feels
that she has abandoned him

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:39.510
and he is thinking about
breaking up with her.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:42.180
In the breakup scene, Junior
is wearing his matching hoodie

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:44.850
but Lexy is not, a sign that
they're no longer in sync

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:45.810
as they once were.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:48.210
We can also see this in the
way that the scene is shot.

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:50.670
The wide lens emphasizes
the distance between them.

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:51.540
And Junior leaves

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:53.160
towards the most destroyed
part of the house.

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:54.420
He's going down a dark path,

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:57.120
leaving Lexy alone in the
middle to choose her direction.

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:59.040
Chucky continues to try to manipulate Jake

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:00.120
into becoming a killer.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:02.820
He taunts him for having missed
his chance to take out Lexy.

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:05.340
- It's called completion anxiety.

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:06.780
- Avid Chucky fans may remember

00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:09.090
where Chucky first learned
about completion anxiety.

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:09.930
It was from Nica,

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:11.670
who had written her
college thesis on the topic

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:14.490
and used it to get under
his skin back in Curse.

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:17.583
- So you never actually
killed Andy Barclay, did you?

00:19:18.518 --> 00:19:19.351
- What?

00:19:19.351 --> 00:19:21.300
- It's called completion anxiety.

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:23.070
It's very common in males.

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:25.680
- Jake does end up relenting
and giving the doll to Lexy,

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:27.270
who uses it to appease her sister.

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:28.590
I don't get why the parents are acting

00:19:28.590 --> 00:19:29.910
like a child's playing with a toy

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:31.320
in the most normal way possible

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:32.970
as some kind of breathtaking thing.

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:35.160
- Great, what's the
little genius doing now?

00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:36.513
- Ssh, look.

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:40.313
- I don't get it.

00:19:40.313 --> 00:19:42.360
She's just playing with
a toy like any kid would.

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:44.820
Caroline's supposed age is
put even more into question

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:47.730
later that day when Lexy
finds her watching TV.

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:49.260
- I thought you're watching "Westworld"?

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:51.270
- Yeah, because Caroline
would absolutely be watching

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:53.700
a very adult-oriented
show like "Westworld".

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:55.110
This line is obviously here,

00:19:55.110 --> 00:19:56.970
not because it makes sense in context,

00:19:56.970 --> 00:19:58.800
but because the creators wanted once again

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.350
to shout-out a show that shares
similarities with Chucky.

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:03.090
Chucky is essentially an animatronic toy

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:04.087
that goes on a rampage.

00:20:04.087 --> 00:20:06.120
"Westworld" is about animatronic humanoids

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:07.320
that go on a rampage.

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:10.320
Junior also brings up
"Westworld" in episode five.

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:13.230
- It's a crazy theme park
with these hot robots

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:15.180
and you can, like, do
anything you want to them.

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:16.500
- Though, it's kind of unclear to me

00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:18.840
if the creators of Chucky
are fans of "Westworld"

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:20.430
or if they're trying to make fun of it,

00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:21.990
because apparently Chucky says

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:24.150
that life is too short to watch it.

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:26.910
- [Caroline] Chucky says life's too short.

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.620
He wants to watch the news.

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:30.660
- That's very familiar to
the first "Child's Play",

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:32.430
where Chucky tells Andy
that he wants to watch

00:20:32.430 --> 00:20:34.500
the nine o'clock news so that
he can listen for updates

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:36.420
about his former accomplice Eddie Caputo.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:37.740
In the case of the TV series,

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:39.150
he's probably keeping his eyes peeled

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:40.680
for stories about Andy Barclay,

00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:42.240
who was recently found to have escaped

00:20:42.240 --> 00:20:43.710
Harrogate Psychiatric Hospital.

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:45.930
It seems like whenever Chucky
is attached to a new kid,

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.700
he brings out his usual bag of tricks

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:48.810
because there's also a line

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:50.430
where Caroline says something horrible

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:51.870
and blames it on Chucky.

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:53.880
- I didn't say it. Chucky did.

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:56.520
- We've heard that before in
"Child's Play" and in "Curse".

00:20:56.520 --> 00:21:00.030
That is the original "Child's
Play", not to the 2019 remake.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:02.190
You've probably noticed that
there aren't many connections

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:03.660
to the 2019 "Child's Play",

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:05.730
and that's because it's
essentially a different series.

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:06.930
It's a fresh continuity.

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:08.700
However, it did play a big role

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:10.680
in a long-standing battle
between the "Chucky" franchise

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:12.517
and the "Toy Story" franchise.

00:21:12.517 --> 00:21:15.120
"Toy Story" is an animated
film about a kid named Andy

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.350
whose toys come to life.

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:18.660
Obviously the similarities
pretty much end there,

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:20.130
but I don't think the
producers of "Chucky"

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:21.480
particularly liked the fact

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:23.610
that the two franchises
share that similarity.

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:24.930
If you're curious, no.

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:25.920
Andy from "Toy Story"

00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:27.900
was not an intentional
"Child's Play" reference.

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:29.610
I guess one of the
original Pixar employees

00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:30.900
had a son named Andy.

00:21:30.900 --> 00:21:32.820
But that didn't stop
Chucky from firing back

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:34.560
during the marketing
campaign for the remake,

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:35.970
which was coming out the same weekend

00:21:35.970 --> 00:21:37.140
as "Toy Story 4".

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:38.970
Interestingly, "Chucky" season one

00:21:38.970 --> 00:21:41.340
keeps the rivalry alive,
not with Andy, though,

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:42.210
but with Chucky.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:43.560
In a flashback to his childhood,

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:45.060
we see the inside of his room.

00:21:45.060 --> 00:21:46.200
Like Andy in "Toy Story",

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:48.750
he has a combination of
astronaut and cowboy stuff.

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:49.950
The hat hanging on his wall

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:51.690
is Jesse's hat from "Toy Story 2".

00:21:51.690 --> 00:21:53.430
He has a View-Master on his nightstand.

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:55.290
The View-Master is a
character in "Toy Story".

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:57.570
And he's got little green
army men on his dresser.

00:21:57.570 --> 00:21:59.040
Also characters from "Toy Story".

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:01.440
When we flashback to
present, Lexy senses danger

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:02.760
and she notices Chucky's feet

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:04.410
poking out from under the window curtain.

00:22:04.410 --> 00:22:06.660
We've seen this once
before in "Cult of Chucky",

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:08.310
but this time it's only a decoy,

00:22:08.310 --> 00:22:10.470
allowing him to sneak up
and make an attempt on her.

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:12.840
It's nice that the series
offers a couple of new twists

00:22:12.840 --> 00:22:14.910
rather than just constantly
repeating moments

00:22:14.910 --> 00:22:15.743
that we've already seen

00:22:15.743 --> 00:22:17.400
in the original seven Chucky movies.

00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:18.750
The last thing we see from that night

00:22:18.750 --> 00:22:20.430
is the headstone of Charles Lee Ray,

00:22:20.430 --> 00:22:22.230
confirming that Jake's dad was indeed

00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:24.600
buried in the same graveyard
we were first introduced to

00:22:24.600 --> 00:22:25.590
in "Bride of Chucky",

00:22:25.590 --> 00:22:27.510
although it looks different
than it did back then.

00:22:27.510 --> 00:22:29.820
My theory is maybe the
original got vandalized

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:31.368
and they had to replace it.

00:22:31.368 --> 00:22:32.940
- [Man] Why do they do it?

00:22:32.940 --> 00:22:34.200
Goddamn kids.

00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:36.450
- [Zac] Episode four begins
at Hackensack Hospital,

00:22:36.450 --> 00:22:37.830
where many characters are recovering

00:22:37.830 --> 00:22:39.870
after Chucky started a
fire at Lexy's party.

00:22:39.870 --> 00:22:42.210
For some reason, it seems
like everyone is being treated

00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:44.760
besides Lexy herself, which
doesn't make sense to me

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:46.890
because she was closest
to where the fire started.

00:22:46.890 --> 00:22:49.350
You would think if anyone got
bronchitis, it would be her.

00:22:49.350 --> 00:22:51.963
But I suppose she did
not have time fo dat.

00:22:53.610 --> 00:22:55.260
- [Jake] Look, anyone who's
told the truth about Chucky

00:22:55.260 --> 00:22:56.850
is either been put away or worse.

00:22:56.850 --> 00:22:57.720
Mostly worse.

00:22:57.720 --> 00:22:59.340
- Just for fun, let's review.

00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:02.040
Who has told the truth about
Chucky and were they put away?

00:23:02.040 --> 00:23:03.690
- Andy Barclay, put away.

00:23:03.690 --> 00:23:05.310
Karen Barclay, put away.

00:23:05.310 --> 00:23:07.080
Lieutenant Preston, dead.

00:23:07.080 --> 00:23:09.810
Jesse and Jade Miller,
alive as far as we know.

00:23:09.810 --> 00:23:12.000
Jennifer Tilly, supernaturally possessed.

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:15.030
Nica Pierce, put away, then
supernaturally possessed.

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:16.950
I'll assume that Kyle, Ronald Tyler,

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:18.690
and Kristen DeSilva kept their mouth shut

00:23:18.690 --> 00:23:20.040
despite knowing about Chucky.

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:22.320
Meanwhile, Devon's mom pays him a visit.

00:23:22.320 --> 00:23:23.223
- I'm a mom.

00:23:24.641 --> 00:23:25.740
I'll be worried the rest of my life.

00:23:25.740 --> 00:23:26.820
- [Zac] Technically true.

00:23:26.820 --> 00:23:28.980
Afterwards, Jake is waiting
for Devon in the hallway

00:23:28.980 --> 00:23:31.110
when a pink soccer ball
is kicked in his direction

00:23:31.110 --> 00:23:32.403
from seemingly no one.

00:23:34.350 --> 00:23:37.620
Naturally, being me, CZsWorld,
I thought about "The Shining"

00:23:37.620 --> 00:23:39.270
when Danny Torrance is
playing in the hallway

00:23:39.270 --> 00:23:40.290
of the Overlook Hotel

00:23:40.290 --> 00:23:42.540
and a pink ball mysteriously
rolled up to him.

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:43.530
At first I wasn't sure

00:23:43.530 --> 00:23:45.360
if they were trying to
reference "The Shining" here,

00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:47.130
but I'm pretty sure it is intentional

00:23:47.130 --> 00:23:48.930
because there are a lot
more "Shining" references

00:23:48.930 --> 00:23:49.763
throughout the season.

00:23:49.763 --> 00:23:52.440
For example, when Tiffany and
Chucky first moved to Chicago

00:23:52.440 --> 00:23:55.110
in the flashback, their
room number is Room 237,

00:23:55.110 --> 00:23:57.720
which is the most haunted
room in the 1980 movie version

00:23:57.720 --> 00:23:58.553
of "The Shining".

00:23:58.553 --> 00:23:59.940
When Chucky breaks into Lexy's house,

00:23:59.940 --> 00:24:03.063
he drops his own take on the
famous "Here's Johnny" line.

00:24:03.063 --> 00:24:05.233
- Here's Chucky.

00:24:05.233 --> 00:24:06.990
- A line that he almost said in Seed,

00:24:06.990 --> 00:24:08.890
but couldn't think of anything to say.

00:24:10.350 --> 00:24:13.110
- I can't think of a thing to say.

00:24:13.110 --> 00:24:15.270
- And in episode eight,
when the army of Chucky's

00:24:15.270 --> 00:24:16.440
is asking the main Chucky

00:24:16.440 --> 00:24:18.360
about which children
are acceptable to kill,

00:24:18.360 --> 00:24:19.650
one of them asks--

00:24:19.650 --> 00:24:20.857
- What about twins?

00:24:20.857 --> 00:24:23.400
- "The Shining" is famous for
showing the graphic mutilation

00:24:23.400 --> 00:24:24.630
of a creepy set of twins,

00:24:24.630 --> 00:24:26.760
and this is immediately
followed up with Chucky laughing

00:24:26.760 --> 00:24:29.175
as we hear the main
theme of "The Shining".

00:24:29.175 --> 00:24:32.390
(laughs sardonically)

00:24:32.390 --> 00:24:35.550
("The Shining" music)

00:24:35.550 --> 00:24:37.770
We hear more music from "The
Shining" during the next scene

00:24:37.770 --> 00:24:38.670
when the army of dolls

00:24:38.670 --> 00:24:40.470
is being loaded into the back of a truck.

00:24:40.470 --> 00:24:42.990
But before we get there,
there is an interesting detail

00:24:42.990 --> 00:24:44.340
on the badges of the employees

00:24:44.340 --> 00:24:46.707
at the Hackensack Memorial Hospital.

00:24:46.707 --> 00:24:49.124
(text thuds)

00:24:51.765 --> 00:24:54.515
(sinister music)

00:24:55.560 --> 00:24:57.540
Given that his mom is
part of the police force,

00:24:57.540 --> 00:24:59.790
Devon finds out that one of
the victims at the party,

00:24:59.790 --> 00:25:01.380
Oliver didn't die in the fire.

00:25:01.380 --> 00:25:03.180
He was actually stabbed to death.

00:25:03.180 --> 00:25:05.910
- Either way there's a
killer out there right now

00:25:05.910 --> 00:25:06.840
running around Hackensack.

00:25:06.840 --> 00:25:09.180
- [Zac] This is the face of a
kid with a true crime podcast,

00:25:09.180 --> 00:25:11.520
trying to act like he's
not excited by that.

00:25:11.520 --> 00:25:13.980
The doctors have to perform
a bronchoscopy on Junior.

00:25:13.980 --> 00:25:15.000
And I noticed that the badges

00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:17.010
worn by the medical staff looked familiar.

00:25:17.010 --> 00:25:18.000
They used the same layout

00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:19.830
as the badges from the
psychiatric hospital

00:25:19.830 --> 00:25:20.730
in "Cult of Chucky".

00:25:20.730 --> 00:25:22.800
I doubt that's something
we're even supposed to notice.

00:25:22.800 --> 00:25:25.500
It's probably just as simple
as they had leftover props

00:25:25.500 --> 00:25:26.370
and storage somewhere,

00:25:26.370 --> 00:25:28.560
but I like that it makes
the world feel cohesive

00:25:28.560 --> 00:25:31.080
so I'm including it in
my already long video.

00:25:31.080 --> 00:25:32.040
To calm his nerves,

00:25:32.040 --> 00:25:34.350
Junior sings "We Got the
Beat" by The Go-Go's.

00:25:34.350 --> 00:25:37.050
Funny how all these Gen Z
middle school kids in 2021

00:25:37.050 --> 00:25:38.520
love all this pop culture stuff

00:25:38.520 --> 00:25:40.200
from the '70s, '80s, and '90s,

00:25:40.200 --> 00:25:42.180
and in some cases even older stuff.

00:25:42.180 --> 00:25:43.650
I already mentioned Lexy singing

00:25:43.650 --> 00:25:45.810
Blue Oyster Cult's 1976 hit,

00:25:45.810 --> 00:25:48.210
Devon watches "Cape Fear" from 1991,

00:25:48.210 --> 00:25:49.807
Jake has a poster from the '80s movie

00:25:49.807 --> 00:25:51.240
"The Outsiders" in his room,

00:25:51.240 --> 00:25:53.130
the mayor plans to donate Good Guy dolls

00:25:53.130 --> 00:25:54.240
to children in need.

00:25:54.240 --> 00:25:56.580
What kid is gonna be excited
about a 33-year-old doll

00:25:56.580 --> 00:25:58.590
that was discontinued over 20 years ago?

00:25:58.590 --> 00:25:59.850
She also does a fundraiser

00:25:59.850 --> 00:26:02.070
by showing the 1931 "Frankenstein".

00:26:02.070 --> 00:26:04.260
They don't even show
90-year-old movies in LA,

00:26:04.260 --> 00:26:05.580
the movie capital of the country,

00:26:05.580 --> 00:26:07.320
there's no way you're
selling out a full-house

00:26:07.320 --> 00:26:09.420
for a "Frankenstein"
screening in New Jersey.

00:26:09.420 --> 00:26:12.300
Jake even compares Chucky to
Teddy Ruxpin at one point.

00:26:12.300 --> 00:26:15.090
Teddy Ruxpin was an actual
animatronic doll from the '80s,

00:26:15.090 --> 00:26:16.500
who, similar to the Good Guy doll,

00:26:16.500 --> 00:26:17.940
had his own cartoon series.

00:26:17.940 --> 00:26:19.650
I think the Good Guy
doll in "Child's Play"

00:26:19.650 --> 00:26:21.810
is inspired 50% by Teddy Ruxpin

00:26:21.810 --> 00:26:23.640
and 50% by the My Buddy doll,

00:26:23.640 --> 00:26:24.600
which I've already talked about

00:26:24.600 --> 00:26:26.310
in my "'Child's Play' Things You Missed".

00:26:26.310 --> 00:26:28.200
I get that Jake is a retro doll collector,

00:26:28.200 --> 00:26:30.660
but there's no way he'd know
about Teddy Ruxpin, come on.

00:26:30.660 --> 00:26:32.310
Also, interesting side note.

00:26:32.310 --> 00:26:34.320
When I was searching for
clips to show on this video,

00:26:34.320 --> 00:26:37.530
I came across this Teddy
Ruxpin commercial from 1985

00:26:37.530 --> 00:26:39.450
where a scientist tries
to bring the doll to life,

00:26:39.450 --> 00:26:40.500
like "Frankenstein".

00:26:40.500 --> 00:26:41.670
I don't think that's necessarily

00:26:41.670 --> 00:26:43.800
why they chose "Frankenstein"
as the movie featured

00:26:43.800 --> 00:26:45.030
in episode seven and eight,

00:26:45.030 --> 00:26:47.400
but I'll get into that when we
get to the end of the season.

00:26:47.400 --> 00:26:48.810
My main point is the only reason

00:26:48.810 --> 00:26:50.640
that the kids in the show
know about '80s stuff

00:26:50.640 --> 00:26:52.770
is because the creators of
the franchise are older now

00:26:52.770 --> 00:26:54.330
and they're putting in references to media

00:26:54.330 --> 00:26:55.470
that influenced them.

00:26:55.470 --> 00:26:56.670
Despite all of this, though,

00:26:56.670 --> 00:26:59.700
Junior does not recognize
Jennifer Tilly from "Bound".

00:26:59.700 --> 00:27:01.980
- Aren't you a little
young to have seen "Bound"?

00:27:01.980 --> 00:27:04.470
- Anyway, Devon gets
bored in his hospital room

00:27:04.470 --> 00:27:06.390
and decides to do some research on Chucky.

00:27:06.390 --> 00:27:08.910
This picture of Tiffany is
literally just a screenshot

00:27:08.910 --> 00:27:09.780
from "Bride of Chucky".

00:27:09.780 --> 00:27:10.613
Like there's no reason

00:27:10.613 --> 00:27:12.720
that this should canonically
exist on the internet.

00:27:12.720 --> 00:27:15.120
They do this a lot in "Saw" so
I won't dwell on it too much,

00:27:15.120 --> 00:27:16.020
but it always bothers me

00:27:16.020 --> 00:27:17.640
that they can just use another picture

00:27:17.640 --> 00:27:19.020
or make something in Photoshop

00:27:19.020 --> 00:27:21.150
or just take a picture
of the younger actress

00:27:21.150 --> 00:27:22.380
playing that same character

00:27:22.380 --> 00:27:24.750
who is literally in this
season in a flashback.

00:27:24.750 --> 00:27:26.430
But before we get to that flashback,

00:27:26.430 --> 00:27:27.930
there's an even earlier flashback

00:27:27.930 --> 00:27:30.600
of Charles Lee Ray's time at
the foster home as a teenager.

00:27:30.600 --> 00:27:32.310
He looks after some of the younger kids

00:27:32.310 --> 00:27:33.810
and they role play "Peter Pan",

00:27:33.810 --> 00:27:36.120
a story about a magical
boy who lives in Neverland,

00:27:36.120 --> 00:27:38.310
a place where children stay young forever

00:27:38.310 --> 00:27:41.280
and they never have to listen
to anyone about anything

00:27:41.280 --> 00:27:43.410
'cause it's all been done
and it's all been said.

00:27:43.410 --> 00:27:45.750
They're the coolest kids and
they take what they can get.

00:27:45.750 --> 00:27:47.940
It's interesting to me
that even at this point

00:27:47.940 --> 00:27:50.160
Charles had this desire for eternal youth,

00:27:50.160 --> 00:27:52.680
because that's basically
what he achieved in 1988

00:27:52.680 --> 00:27:55.140
by transferring his soul into
the body of a Good Guy doll

00:27:55.140 --> 00:27:57.060
forever giving him the form of a child.

00:27:57.060 --> 00:27:58.710
Charles leads the kids to stumble upon

00:27:58.710 --> 00:28:01.260
the body of the janitor, who
he refers to as Captain Hook,

00:28:01.260 --> 00:28:03.540
and everyone runs away except for one boy,

00:28:03.540 --> 00:28:05.310
who we later found out to be Eddie Caputo,

00:28:05.310 --> 00:28:07.200
the man who is supposed to
be Charles's getaway driver

00:28:07.200 --> 00:28:09.450
the night he was killed in
the opening of "Child's Play".

00:28:09.450 --> 00:28:10.470
But back in the present,

00:28:10.470 --> 00:28:12.240
Lexy and Jake are
searching the burned house

00:28:12.240 --> 00:28:14.423
for the remnants of Chucky.
- What are you waiting for?

00:28:14.423 --> 00:28:15.330
- I don't know where your room is.

00:28:15.330 --> 00:28:17.490
- Bet he's the only boy in
the school who can say that.

00:28:17.490 --> 00:28:19.020
- Oh!

00:28:19.020 --> 00:28:20.970
- A detective comes by, discovers Chucky,

00:28:20.970 --> 00:28:23.250
and refers to him as an ugly f***ing doll.

00:28:23.250 --> 00:28:25.250
I think this is a callback
to the woman who finds Chucky

00:28:25.250 --> 00:28:27.750
in the elevator back in the
original "Child's Play".

00:28:27.750 --> 00:28:29.040
- Ugly doll.

00:28:29.040 --> 00:28:31.080
- Before long I'm pretty
sure every single moment

00:28:31.080 --> 00:28:32.730
from the original movie
will have come back

00:28:32.730 --> 00:28:34.320
as some kind of Easter egg or reference

00:28:34.320 --> 00:28:35.490
if they keep this series up.

00:28:35.490 --> 00:28:37.500
Like, for example, how in the original

00:28:37.500 --> 00:28:39.000
Andy wears Good Guys pajamas;

00:28:39.000 --> 00:28:40.800
and in the show we eventually come across

00:28:40.800 --> 00:28:43.080
the pink soccer ball kid
and he's wearing overalls

00:28:43.080 --> 00:28:44.280
on top of a striped shirt.

00:28:44.280 --> 00:28:46.080
His outfit resembles the Good Guys outfit,

00:28:46.080 --> 00:28:47.220
but the colors are different.

00:28:47.220 --> 00:28:48.660
And now is the perfect time to tell you

00:28:48.660 --> 00:28:49.650
that you can buy this mer--

00:28:49.650 --> 00:28:51.600
when the detective brings
Chucky back to Caroline,

00:28:51.600 --> 00:28:54.060
he gets distracted by food
and eats a powdered donut

00:28:54.060 --> 00:28:55.380
right over the killer doll.

00:28:55.380 --> 00:28:57.840
The result is white powder
falling down onto Chucky.

00:28:57.840 --> 00:28:59.700
And I'm pretty sure this is no accident,

00:28:59.700 --> 00:29:01.920
as this is kind of a running
theme in the franchise.

00:29:01.920 --> 00:29:04.800
The snow in "Child's Play",
the fluff in "Curse of Chucky",

00:29:04.800 --> 00:29:06.270
then more snow in "Cult of Chucky".

00:29:06.270 --> 00:29:08.730
They're constantly recreating
that wintery image.

00:29:08.730 --> 00:29:10.560
Given that we're in a
hospital on this episode,

00:29:10.560 --> 00:29:12.240
there are obviously gonna
be a lot of callbacks

00:29:12.240 --> 00:29:14.490
to "Cult of Chucky", which
similarly takes place

00:29:14.490 --> 00:29:15.810
in a mental hospital.

00:29:15.810 --> 00:29:17.760
- God, I love hospitals.

00:29:17.760 --> 00:29:18.870
- We know you do, Chucky.

00:29:18.870 --> 00:29:20.910
But we can't forget that
there's also a hospital scene

00:29:20.910 --> 00:29:21.743
in the original.

00:29:21.743 --> 00:29:23.340
It's definitely a familiar territory.

00:29:23.340 --> 00:29:26.597
So Chucky knows just where
to find some dangerous items.

00:29:26.597 --> 00:29:29.190
- You might feel a little prick.

00:29:29.190 --> 00:29:30.750
- This one actually comes from the poster

00:29:30.750 --> 00:29:31.710
for "Cult of Chucky".

00:29:31.710 --> 00:29:33.930
Although I don't think it's
ever actually said in the movie.

00:29:33.930 --> 00:29:36.360
Jake and Lexy eventually
decide to see what Devon knows

00:29:36.360 --> 00:29:38.790
about the Lakeshore Strangler
and he brings up a good point.

00:29:38.790 --> 00:29:40.859
- He never really strangled anyone.

00:29:40.859 --> 00:29:42.177
I mean, he was more of
like a mangler or a--

00:29:42.177 --> 00:29:43.140
- Devon!

00:29:43.140 --> 00:29:44.580
- This is before Devon finds out

00:29:44.580 --> 00:29:46.140
that the legend of the cursed Chucky doll

00:29:46.140 --> 00:29:47.640
is more than an urban legend,

00:29:47.640 --> 00:29:49.380
because we have seen Chucky as a doll

00:29:49.380 --> 00:29:51.660
strangle people on several occasions.

00:29:51.660 --> 00:29:53.760
- Nothin' like his strangulation

00:29:53.760 --> 00:29:55.890
to get the circulation going.

00:29:55.890 --> 00:29:57.690
- But the fact that Devon
is the one to bring up

00:29:57.690 --> 00:29:58.830
this point about strangling,

00:29:58.830 --> 00:30:00.600
it might be a dark foreshadowing

00:30:00.600 --> 00:30:03.000
as it would be his own mom
who is strangled by Chucky

00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:04.020
later in the story.

00:30:04.020 --> 00:30:06.060
Meanwhile, Jake, still a prime suspect

00:30:06.060 --> 00:30:08.700
for the recent murders, is
interrogated by Detective Evans.

00:30:08.700 --> 00:30:10.860
Pretty sure you need a
parent or a guardian present

00:30:10.860 --> 00:30:13.110
to question a minor, Mrs. Evans.

00:30:13.110 --> 00:30:14.880
Lucky for both of them, I guess,

00:30:14.880 --> 00:30:17.340
they're interrupted by a
disturbance from Caroline's room.

00:30:17.340 --> 00:30:18.960
Chucky had pulled the plug on this machine

00:30:18.960 --> 00:30:21.390
giving her oxygen, which I
find it very hard to believe

00:30:21.390 --> 00:30:23.250
that a device like this
wouldn't have any form

00:30:23.250 --> 00:30:25.470
of battery backup, but
everyone freaks out,

00:30:25.470 --> 00:30:26.760
especially Mrs. Cross.

00:30:26.760 --> 00:30:28.320
I'm pretty sure we're
supposed to get the idea

00:30:28.320 --> 00:30:29.280
that she's in a panic,

00:30:29.280 --> 00:30:31.387
because they keep playing
the same audio of her saying,

00:30:31.387 --> 00:30:32.250
"Please hurry."

00:30:32.250 --> 00:30:36.000
- Please hurry. Please
hurry, please hurry.

00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:37.590
- She sounds like you guys

00:30:37.590 --> 00:30:39.300
trying to get me to finish this video.

00:30:39.300 --> 00:30:40.650
Another common request I get

00:30:40.650 --> 00:30:42.900
is people asking me to
make more "Saw" content.

00:30:42.900 --> 00:30:45.060
I will at some point, but you
don't have to wait that long

00:30:45.060 --> 00:30:47.280
because there are a couple of
"Saw" Easter eggs right here

00:30:47.280 --> 00:30:49.417
in the next episode of Chucky.

00:30:49.417 --> 00:30:51.834
(text thuds)

00:30:54.388 --> 00:30:56.460
(sinister music)

00:30:56.460 --> 00:30:59.040
The fifth episode would be
titled "Little Little Lies".

00:30:59.040 --> 00:31:01.830
It starts a trend of episode
names that parody other works.

00:31:01.830 --> 00:31:03.690
In this case, the show "Big Little Lies"

00:31:03.690 --> 00:31:05.490
or perhaps the book that it's based on.

00:31:05.490 --> 00:31:07.770
Chucky once again proclaims
his love of hospitals

00:31:07.770 --> 00:31:10.260
as he swims around in a
dump of discarded needles.

00:31:10.260 --> 00:31:12.330
This isn't the first time
that I've talked about someone

00:31:12.330 --> 00:31:13.620
rummaging through a needle pit

00:31:13.620 --> 00:31:16.170
as this is also something
that happens in "Saw II".

00:31:16.170 --> 00:31:18.420
Ever since "Scream" first came
out and started the trend,

00:31:18.420 --> 00:31:20.130
Chucky has followed suit by referencing

00:31:20.130 --> 00:31:22.560
as many other popular horror
properties as possible.

00:31:22.560 --> 00:31:24.060
But I believe this is the first "Saw"

00:31:24.060 --> 00:31:25.200
reference for the Chuck.

00:31:25.200 --> 00:31:26.910
We wouldn't have to wait
long for the second.

00:31:26.910 --> 00:31:29.130
At the Hotel Hackensack
later in this episode,

00:31:29.130 --> 00:31:30.780
we see a bald guy in a white t-shirt

00:31:30.780 --> 00:31:32.250
lying face down in a puddle.

00:31:32.250 --> 00:31:33.870
He looks exactly like John Kramer

00:31:33.870 --> 00:31:35.370
when we see him in "Saw" one.

00:31:35.370 --> 00:31:37.500
A few days later, class
is back in session.

00:31:37.500 --> 00:31:39.600
And in science, the lesson is about biotic

00:31:39.600 --> 00:31:40.950
and abiotic factors.

00:31:40.950 --> 00:31:43.170
In other words, living
and non-living elements

00:31:43.170 --> 00:31:44.160
of our ecosystem.

00:31:44.160 --> 00:31:45.150
It seems appropriate

00:31:45.150 --> 00:31:47.490
because Jake, Lexy, and Devon's
biggest hurdle right now

00:31:47.490 --> 00:31:48.720
is getting people to realize

00:31:48.720 --> 00:31:50.670
that the Chucky doll is actually alive,

00:31:50.670 --> 00:31:52.020
which makes "Chucky" episode five

00:31:52.020 --> 00:31:54.000
kinda feel like "Harry
Potter" number five,

00:31:54.000 --> 00:31:55.800
but that's definitely a coincidence.

00:31:55.800 --> 00:31:57.780
Given that Chucky's face
got melted in the fire,

00:31:57.780 --> 00:31:59.700
Nathan gets Caroline a new Good Guy doll.

00:31:59.700 --> 00:32:02.130
- Hi, I'm Tommy.

00:32:02.130 --> 00:32:04.470
- This is another callback
to "Child's Play 2",

00:32:04.470 --> 00:32:05.550
where Andy's foster parents

00:32:05.550 --> 00:32:07.350
happen to have a Good
Guy doll named Tommy,

00:32:07.350 --> 00:32:09.000
which Chucky buries in the backyard.

00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:10.740
There are 50 different
names for Good Guy dolls

00:32:10.740 --> 00:32:12.750
and Chucky and Tommy are two of them.

00:32:12.750 --> 00:32:14.460
That evening, there's a lightning storm.

00:32:14.460 --> 00:32:16.440
If you've been with the
Chucky franchise for a while,

00:32:16.440 --> 00:32:17.400
you know what this means.

00:32:17.400 --> 00:32:19.890
But if you're new, you may
not realize this is a clue

00:32:19.890 --> 00:32:21.960
that the doll Jake,
Devon, and Lexy destroy

00:32:21.960 --> 00:32:23.460
is no longer the real Chucky.

00:32:23.460 --> 00:32:24.600
Ever since the first movie,

00:32:24.600 --> 00:32:26.220
the sign that Chucky
has transferred his soul

00:32:26.220 --> 00:32:28.440
into a new body is the
appearance of storm clouds

00:32:28.440 --> 00:32:29.760
and a great strike of lightning.

00:32:29.760 --> 00:32:31.920
Part of a ritual called
the Damballa Chant.

00:32:31.920 --> 00:32:32.910
Over at the Wheeler house,

00:32:32.910 --> 00:32:34.770
Junior's dad is working
on getting him a trainer

00:32:34.770 --> 00:32:37.133
for cross-country nationals.
- [Logan] In a week or two

00:32:37.133 --> 00:32:39.780
we're gonna have you
back out there runnin'.

00:32:39.780 --> 00:32:41.100
I even got you a trainer.

00:32:41.100 --> 00:32:43.200
That guy Dobbs. The best.

00:32:43.200 --> 00:32:44.850
- We never see or meets Dobbs

00:32:44.850 --> 00:32:47.610
so it feels oddly specific
that he's mentioned by name.

00:32:47.610 --> 00:32:48.780
I'm gonna go out on a limb here

00:32:48.780 --> 00:32:51.210
and say that this might be a
reference to a movie character.

00:32:51.210 --> 00:32:53.070
Our "Child's Play" from 1988

00:32:53.070 --> 00:32:55.170
was not the first movie
called "Child's Play".

00:32:55.170 --> 00:32:58.620
In 1972, a mystery film called
"Child's Play" was released

00:32:58.620 --> 00:33:00.510
and it was based off a
play of the same name.

00:33:00.510 --> 00:33:02.640
The main character is
named at Joseph Dobbs.

00:33:02.640 --> 00:33:04.260
Maybe this is a reference to that.

00:33:04.260 --> 00:33:05.430
Also. I just wanna add.

00:33:05.430 --> 00:33:07.110
I love the implication that Lexy's mom

00:33:07.110 --> 00:33:08.640
doesn't know how to operate the dishwasher

00:33:08.640 --> 00:33:09.600
without the maid around.

00:33:09.600 --> 00:33:10.710
No surprise there.

00:33:10.710 --> 00:33:12.450
This is the episode where we finally see

00:33:12.450 --> 00:33:13.920
where Chucky first met Tiffany.

00:33:13.920 --> 00:33:16.050
He walks over to her table and asks.

00:33:16.050 --> 00:33:17.860
- Hey, Red. What's new?

00:33:17.860 --> 00:33:19.737
- She's not the only one to be called Red.

00:33:19.737 --> 00:33:22.590
In "Seed of Chucky", Jennifer
Tilly pursues a relationship

00:33:22.590 --> 00:33:25.440
with the rapper producer
known as Redman and says--

00:33:25.440 --> 00:33:26.910
- Thank you, Mr. Man.

00:33:26.910 --> 00:33:28.410
Oh, could I call you Red?

00:33:28.410 --> 00:33:29.580
- In Tiffany's case, however,

00:33:29.580 --> 00:33:32.070
Charles may be calling her
red because she has red hair.

00:33:32.070 --> 00:33:33.000
You just can't really tell

00:33:33.000 --> 00:33:34.590
because there's a red light cast on her

00:33:34.590 --> 00:33:37.080
in both of the scenes she's
in before she goes blonde.

00:33:37.080 --> 00:33:38.730
We jump forward to present day,

00:33:38.730 --> 00:33:40.680
where Chucky and Tiffany
are back making love

00:33:40.680 --> 00:33:42.720
in the same hotel, both
in different bodies

00:33:42.720 --> 00:33:43.740
than they were in the '80s.

00:33:43.740 --> 00:33:45.420
That's not me saying that they got fat,

00:33:45.420 --> 00:33:47.070
like they're literally
in different bodies.

00:33:47.070 --> 00:33:49.530
But in reality, Tiffany did
happen to gain some weight

00:33:49.530 --> 00:33:51.420
and Chucky criticizes her eating habits.

00:33:51.420 --> 00:33:53.077
So she fires back at him with one of her

00:33:53.077 --> 00:33:54.960
"My mother always told me" catchphrases,

00:33:54.960 --> 00:33:56.190
something that she's been pulling out

00:33:56.190 --> 00:33:57.690
since we first met her in Bride.

00:33:57.690 --> 00:33:59.640
There's another sneaky
reference to "Bride of Chucky"

00:33:59.640 --> 00:34:02.280
as Principal McVey greets
everybody coming into the assembly

00:34:02.280 --> 00:34:03.720
at the school auditorium.

00:34:03.720 --> 00:34:05.190
- Hey, can we expect those famous

00:34:05.190 --> 00:34:07.980
everything but the sink cookies this year?

00:34:07.980 --> 00:34:08.813
Great.

00:34:08.813 --> 00:34:11.220
- Not knowing what everything
but the sink cookies are,

00:34:11.220 --> 00:34:13.530
I looked it up and discovered
it's the name of a recipe

00:34:13.530 --> 00:34:14.940
created by Martha Stewart,

00:34:14.940 --> 00:34:17.010
the TV personality who Tiffany idolized

00:34:17.010 --> 00:34:19.302
throughout "Bride of
Chucky"..... until the end.

00:34:19.302 --> 00:34:20.760
- **** Martha Stewart!

00:34:20.760 --> 00:34:22.680
- [Zac] I noticed that each
of the seats in the auditorium

00:34:22.680 --> 00:34:23.640
have labels on them.

00:34:23.640 --> 00:34:25.380
I'm guessing this is
just the way things were

00:34:25.380 --> 00:34:27.000
at the location where they filmed this,

00:34:27.000 --> 00:34:29.017
but I couldn't help but
notice that one of them says

00:34:29.017 --> 00:34:29.910
"Barber's Chair".

00:34:29.910 --> 00:34:31.860
One of Chucky's victims
in "Child's Play 3"

00:34:31.860 --> 00:34:33.270
was killed in a barber's chair.

00:34:33.270 --> 00:34:35.070
However, I'm gonna call this a coincidence

00:34:35.070 --> 00:34:37.050
because all of the other
chairs have labels on them

00:34:37.050 --> 00:34:39.150
and none of them have any
significant meaning to me

00:34:39.150 --> 00:34:40.710
as a Chucky franchise viewer.

00:34:40.710 --> 00:34:42.450
Thought it would just be
a fun thing to mention.

00:34:42.450 --> 00:34:43.710
Much like how I think it's fun

00:34:43.710 --> 00:34:45.340
that they had the balls to put a meme song

00:34:45.340 --> 00:34:46.770
in a "Chucky" episode.

00:34:46.770 --> 00:34:48.090
This guy's going viral.

00:34:48.090 --> 00:34:49.470
Get this on the trending page.

00:34:49.470 --> 00:34:51.000
Don't worry, I blurred it out.

00:34:51.000 --> 00:34:52.860
Episode six is called "Cape Queer",

00:34:52.860 --> 00:34:54.360
a parody of the movie "Cape Fear",

00:34:54.360 --> 00:34:55.800
which Devon can be seen watching

00:34:55.800 --> 00:34:57.270
and he takes inspiration from.

00:34:57.270 --> 00:34:58.650
And we are finally reintroduced

00:34:58.650 --> 00:35:00.510
to the man himself, Andy Barclay.

00:35:00.510 --> 00:35:02.220
So in the last episode, Nica was told

00:35:02.220 --> 00:35:03.720
that the date is November eighth.

00:35:03.720 --> 00:35:05.550
This episode looks to be on the next day.

00:35:05.550 --> 00:35:06.383
We don't know for sure,

00:35:06.383 --> 00:35:08.100
but we can kind of assume
that it's the next day

00:35:08.100 --> 00:35:10.530
which would be November
9th, Andy's birthday.

00:35:10.530 --> 00:35:12.810
Andy was first introduced
on his sixth birthday,

00:35:12.810 --> 00:35:15.240
reintroduced the day
before his 31st birthday,

00:35:15.240 --> 00:35:18.120
and now we would be meeting
him again on his 39th birthday.

00:35:18.120 --> 00:35:19.980
Andy and Kyle go to investigate a house

00:35:19.980 --> 00:35:21.360
where they suspect Chucky might be.

00:35:21.360 --> 00:35:23.310
And when this little
girl brings out her doll,

00:35:23.310 --> 00:35:25.680
you can see the burnt fingers
on Chucky's right hand.

00:35:25.680 --> 00:35:27.690
This tells us that this
is the very same doll

00:35:27.690 --> 00:35:28.590
from "Cult of Chucky",

00:35:28.590 --> 00:35:30.720
which Nika had Dr. Foley
hold a lighter up to

00:35:30.720 --> 00:35:32.550
in an attempt to prove
that it was just a doll,

00:35:32.550 --> 00:35:34.200
which of course was unsuccessful.

00:35:34.200 --> 00:35:36.510
This means that Andy and
Kyle are still hunting down

00:35:36.510 --> 00:35:38.310
the remaining fragments of Chucky's soul.

00:35:38.310 --> 00:35:41.400
A male-female soul hunting
duo? Sounds familiar.

00:35:41.400 --> 00:35:42.900
At the end of Cult, we can assume

00:35:42.900 --> 00:35:44.910
that buzz cut and no bod are dead,

00:35:44.910 --> 00:35:47.640
leaving hot hands, Nica
Chucky, and cope Chucky.

00:35:47.640 --> 00:35:49.560
But hot hands is taken out in episode six,

00:35:49.560 --> 00:35:51.780
which leaves just Nica
Chucky and cope Chucky,

00:35:51.780 --> 00:35:54.060
who is presumably the
one that belongs to Jake.

00:35:54.060 --> 00:35:55.470
Not that any of this matters

00:35:55.470 --> 00:35:57.360
because they'll never
kill the last Chucky off,

00:35:57.360 --> 00:35:59.040
but I just find it fun to sort out.

00:35:59.040 --> 00:36:00.510
With Jake's name mostly cleared,

00:36:00.510 --> 00:36:02.550
the police arrest Mrs. Fairchild...

00:36:02.550 --> 00:36:04.380
in the middle of her science class?

00:36:04.380 --> 00:36:06.240
They couldn't have just asked
her for a word in the hall

00:36:06.240 --> 00:36:08.460
instead of arresting her in
front of all of the students?

00:36:08.460 --> 00:36:09.990
Especially when they don't even have proof

00:36:09.990 --> 00:36:11.460
that Ms. Fairchild is guilty?

00:36:11.460 --> 00:36:12.420
I'm really starting to doubt

00:36:12.420 --> 00:36:14.400
Detective Evan's abilities as a cop.

00:36:14.400 --> 00:36:16.740
This girl's just happy winter
break came early this year.

00:36:16.740 --> 00:36:18.210
I love how the editor tried to get away

00:36:18.210 --> 00:36:19.890
with using the same hotel exterior

00:36:19.890 --> 00:36:22.140
in episode five and six by
just putting a car there

00:36:22.140 --> 00:36:23.130
in episode five.

00:36:23.130 --> 00:36:24.570
Anyway, we come in on Tiffany

00:36:24.570 --> 00:36:26.130
who is busy trying to close a suitcase

00:36:26.130 --> 00:36:27.360
filled with human remains.

00:36:27.360 --> 00:36:29.130
In "Bride of Chucky",
she had the same problem

00:36:29.130 --> 00:36:30.120
with her storage chest,

00:36:30.120 --> 00:36:32.310
which accidentally still had
Damien's hair sticking out

00:36:32.310 --> 00:36:34.470
shortly before she got help
loading it into her car.

00:36:34.470 --> 00:36:37.110
She gets frustrated
with Chucky and screams.

00:36:37.110 --> 00:36:39.150
- Get your leg off my suitcase!

00:36:39.150 --> 00:36:40.710
- Before chopping down with a cleaver.

00:36:40.710 --> 00:36:42.240
And although she wasn't
actually attempting

00:36:42.240 --> 00:36:43.350
to chop Nica's leg off,

00:36:43.350 --> 00:36:45.420
this is kind of a
preview of things to come

00:36:45.420 --> 00:36:48.180
because she does later end up
removing all of Nica's limbs

00:36:48.180 --> 00:36:49.230
so that she can't get away

00:36:49.230 --> 00:36:50.910
even if Chucky takes over her body.

00:36:50.910 --> 00:36:53.580
I have more to say about this,
but I'll save it for later.

00:36:53.580 --> 00:36:56.310
This episode also features
more flashback material.

00:36:56.310 --> 00:36:59.070
And this one scene shows
off the origin of not three,

00:36:59.070 --> 00:37:01.830
but four iconic elements
that fans have come to love

00:37:01.830 --> 00:37:03.686
in the Chucky franchise.

00:37:03.686 --> 00:37:06.101
(thunder rumbles)

00:37:06.101 --> 00:37:08.747
(thunder clasp)

00:37:08.747 --> 00:37:11.497
(sinister music)

00:37:12.480 --> 00:37:14.130
In a flashback to 1987,

00:37:14.130 --> 00:37:16.890
we see a younger Chucky and
Tiffany purchasing a Pontiac.

00:37:16.890 --> 00:37:19.560
And when I say purchasing,
I mean, obtaining

00:37:19.560 --> 00:37:21.123
This car is not a big part of the series.

00:37:21.123 --> 00:37:23.640
It's not something you would
necessarily even notice,

00:37:23.640 --> 00:37:25.380
but I like that they
included it in the scene

00:37:25.380 --> 00:37:27.660
because Tiffany still has
it over a decade later

00:37:27.660 --> 00:37:28.650
in "Bride of Chucky".

00:37:28.650 --> 00:37:30.870
But it's never driven because
she turns into a doll.

00:37:30.870 --> 00:37:32.790
We do see it again,
though, in "Cult of Chucky"

00:37:32.790 --> 00:37:34.050
as the car that Chucky and Tiffany

00:37:34.050 --> 00:37:35.640
make their getaway from the asylum in.

00:37:35.640 --> 00:37:38.610
The color is described as
Coronado Red, which Tiffany loves,

00:37:38.610 --> 00:37:40.170
probably 'cause it'll be less noticeable

00:37:40.170 --> 00:37:41.310
when blood gets on it.

00:37:41.310 --> 00:37:43.230
This also marks the first
time chronologically

00:37:43.230 --> 00:37:45.750
that she uses her signature
weapon, her nail file.

00:37:45.750 --> 00:37:48.360
But there's even more that
originates from this scene.

00:37:48.360 --> 00:37:50.670
Roll it.
(text swooshes)

00:37:50.670 --> 00:37:52.590
- It's a stunning automobile.

00:37:52.590 --> 00:37:55.140
And a true classic
never goes out of style.

00:37:55.140 --> 00:37:56.220
- What'd you say?

00:37:56.220 --> 00:37:58.080
- The car wasn't the
only thing Chucky stole,

00:37:58.080 --> 00:37:59.430
as he would also claim this line

00:37:59.430 --> 00:38:01.410
as one of his many catch phrases.

00:38:01.410 --> 00:38:05.250
- A true classic never goes out of style.

00:38:05.250 --> 00:38:07.950
- A true classic never goes out of style.

00:38:07.950 --> 00:38:10.290
- Then he makes this clarification.

00:38:10.290 --> 00:38:13.581
- [Charles] Technically,
it isn't even an antique.

00:38:13.581 --> 00:38:15.081
- (chuckles) Well, sure it is.

00:38:16.020 --> 00:38:18.450
It's vintage and retro.

00:38:18.450 --> 00:38:21.750
- This calls all the way
back to, well, episode one,

00:38:21.750 --> 00:38:24.480
where Jake uses this distinction
between vintage and retro

00:38:24.480 --> 00:38:25.950
to haggle the price of the doll.

00:38:25.950 --> 00:38:27.010
- What's the difference?

00:38:27.010 --> 00:38:28.230
- About 10 bucks.

00:38:28.230 --> 00:38:30.540
- Then after stealing the
car, Chucky kicks back

00:38:30.540 --> 00:38:32.220
and reads from "The
Ultimate Book of Voodoo",

00:38:32.220 --> 00:38:33.630
which presumably marks the beginning

00:38:33.630 --> 00:38:36.000
of his interest in voodoo in
order to transfer his soul

00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:37.680
into another body to beat death.

00:38:37.680 --> 00:38:39.360
Back in the present, Tiffany tests to see

00:38:39.360 --> 00:38:41.070
if Chucky or Nica is in control

00:38:41.070 --> 00:38:43.050
by asking about their
honeymoon in Niagara.

00:38:43.050 --> 00:38:44.250
Nica wasn't there for this,

00:38:44.250 --> 00:38:45.990
so she's calling her
bluff in the poker game

00:38:45.990 --> 00:38:48.840
while simultaneously calling
her bluff in the conversation

00:38:48.840 --> 00:38:49.980
in the situation.

00:38:49.980 --> 00:38:51.090
After knocking Nica out,

00:38:51.090 --> 00:38:53.610
she picks up the keys to her
recently purchased house.

00:38:53.610 --> 00:38:55.200
And of course, she's got the same car

00:38:55.200 --> 00:38:56.850
and she's buying Chucky's old house.

00:38:56.850 --> 00:38:58.650
I guess she's basking in the nostalgia,

00:38:58.650 --> 00:39:00.060
but I'm not sure how to feel about her

00:39:00.060 --> 00:39:01.350
not being goth anymore.

00:39:01.350 --> 00:39:02.437
This is goth erasure.

00:39:02.437 --> 00:39:04.530
#stopgotherasure.

00:39:04.530 --> 00:39:05.850
If you look on the For Sale sign,

00:39:05.850 --> 00:39:08.460
you'll see that the realtor's
name is Gladys Kravitz.

00:39:08.460 --> 00:39:09.840
She shares a name with a character

00:39:09.840 --> 00:39:11.970
from the 1960s sitcom "Bewitched".

00:39:11.970 --> 00:39:13.980
Her character is
portrayed by Alice Pierce,

00:39:13.980 --> 00:39:16.710
who shares a name with Alice
Pierce from "Curse of Chucky".

00:39:16.710 --> 00:39:18.150
What is the reason for these characters

00:39:18.150 --> 00:39:20.100
being named in connection
with "Bewitched"?

00:39:20.100 --> 00:39:21.360
It's not really clear.

00:39:21.360 --> 00:39:23.310
I'm guessing Don Mancini is just a fan.

00:39:23.310 --> 00:39:24.630
He actually brought up the show once

00:39:24.630 --> 00:39:26.100
in an interview with Forbes.

00:39:26.100 --> 00:39:28.710
Around this time, Andy and
Kyle are in Richmond, Virginia

00:39:28.710 --> 00:39:30.630
where Jake and his friends
make contact with them

00:39:30.630 --> 00:39:32.970
and Andy welcomes them to
the lucky group of survivors

00:39:32.970 --> 00:39:33.870
who know about Chucky.

00:39:33.870 --> 00:39:36.870
Just for fun, that group would
include Andy, Karen Barclay,

00:39:36.870 --> 00:39:39.270
Detective Mike Norris,
Detective Jack Santos,

00:39:39.270 --> 00:39:42.360
Kyle, Kristin DeSilva,
Ronald Tyler, Major Ellis,

00:39:42.360 --> 00:39:44.790
Jesse and Jade Miller, and Nica Pierce.

00:39:44.790 --> 00:39:46.440
Let me know if you can
think of any others.

00:39:46.440 --> 00:39:49.050
One character who is not
so lucky is Bree Wheeler.

00:39:49.050 --> 00:39:50.280
She gets knocked out of the window

00:39:50.280 --> 00:39:51.750
of a high-rise building by Chucky,

00:39:51.750 --> 00:39:54.330
a direct callback to the
first kill of the first movie.

00:39:54.330 --> 00:39:56.850
Both of these characters are
the main character's aunt.

00:39:56.850 --> 00:39:58.350
We also saw an aunt character fall

00:39:58.350 --> 00:39:59.820
from a great height in Curse.

00:39:59.820 --> 00:40:01.740
I guess if you have a niece
or nephew in the series,

00:40:01.740 --> 00:40:03.780
get ready to take some fall damage.

00:40:03.780 --> 00:40:06.420
The song that plays during the
scene is called "Trampoline".

00:40:06.420 --> 00:40:08.670
I guess Bree really
could've used one here.

00:40:08.670 --> 00:40:09.503
There are a couple more

00:40:09.503 --> 00:40:11.400
"Child's Play"-esque
references that evening

00:40:11.400 --> 00:40:13.830
when the trio sets a trap
for Chucky in Logan's house.

00:40:13.830 --> 00:40:16.200
Chucky gets around this by
sneaking in through the chimney,

00:40:16.200 --> 00:40:18.150
thereby leaving tiny
footprints in the dust

00:40:18.150 --> 00:40:20.640
near the fireplace, just like
he did in the spilled flour

00:40:20.640 --> 00:40:22.230
back in Karen Barclay's kitchen.

00:40:22.230 --> 00:40:24.390
He proceeds to turn on
all the gas in the house,

00:40:24.390 --> 00:40:26.490
the same tactic that he
used in Eddie Caputo's house

00:40:26.490 --> 00:40:27.540
before blowing it up.

00:40:27.540 --> 00:40:29.280
I don't know if it would
actually work this time

00:40:29.280 --> 00:40:30.480
because he left the flame on.

00:40:30.480 --> 00:40:32.190
I'm pretty sure it's
only when the gas is on

00:40:32.190 --> 00:40:33.810
without a flame when you have to worry.

00:40:33.810 --> 00:40:35.940
Episode six ends with
the death of Devon's mom.

00:40:35.940 --> 00:40:37.800
And with the body count
really piling up now,

00:40:37.800 --> 00:40:39.120
the intro of episode seven

00:40:39.120 --> 00:40:40.530
fittingly shows the "Chucky" logo

00:40:40.530 --> 00:40:42.660
made up of the gravestones
of many of the victims

00:40:42.660 --> 00:40:44.010
of the Chucky franchise.

00:40:44.010 --> 00:40:45.960
They aren't just victims
from this season, though;

00:40:45.960 --> 00:40:48.300
they're victims from the
entire history of Chucky.

00:40:48.300 --> 00:40:51.390
They include Howard
Fitzwater AKA Damien Baylock,

00:40:51.390 --> 00:40:53.460
Tiffany's goth boyfriend
from "Bride of Chucky";

00:40:53.460 --> 00:40:55.950
Sarah Pierce, Nica's mother
from "Curse of Chucky";

00:40:55.950 --> 00:40:58.710
Grace Poole, Andy's social
worker from "Child's Play 2";

00:40:58.710 --> 00:41:00.750
Tony Gardner, the movie's
special effects guy

00:41:00.750 --> 00:41:02.340
from "Seed of Chucky", who, by the way,

00:41:02.340 --> 00:41:03.960
is also the actual puppeteer

00:41:03.960 --> 00:41:05.460
and a producer for the franchise.

00:41:05.460 --> 00:41:07.710
His appearance in "Seed of
Chucky" is actually a cameo.

00:41:07.710 --> 00:41:09.840
Sean Peyton, the police
officer who is stabbed

00:41:09.840 --> 00:41:11.430
with the syringes in episode four.

00:41:11.430 --> 00:41:13.470
Eddie Caputo, Charles Lee Ray's accomplice

00:41:13.470 --> 00:41:15.150
and getaway driver in "Child's Play".

00:41:15.150 --> 00:41:17.970
Warren Kincaid, the police
officer and father of Jade

00:41:17.970 --> 00:41:18.960
in "Bride of Chucky".

00:41:18.960 --> 00:41:22.020
Redman, the rapper/movie
producer from "Seed of Chucky".

00:41:22.020 --> 00:41:23.970
Francis Martinez, we can only assume

00:41:23.970 --> 00:41:25.950
that this is Father Frank
from "Curse of Chucky".

00:41:25.950 --> 00:41:27.990
Frank is sometimes used
as a nickname for Francis

00:41:27.990 --> 00:41:30.960
and he was Hispanic, so the
last name Martinez kind of fits.

00:41:30.960 --> 00:41:33.540
Philip Simpson, the foster
father from "Child's Play 2",

00:41:33.540 --> 00:41:34.650
and Joanne Simpson,

00:41:34.650 --> 00:41:36.510
the foster mother from "Child's Play 2".

00:41:36.510 --> 00:41:38.160
Due to the stress of losing his wife

00:41:38.160 --> 00:41:39.720
and all of the strange circumstances

00:41:39.720 --> 00:41:42.390
of the things going on around
him, Logan takes to drinking.

00:41:42.390 --> 00:41:44.250
When he gets up, we get a
clear look at the bottle

00:41:44.250 --> 00:41:45.900
of Kentucky bourbon that he's working on.

00:41:45.900 --> 00:41:47.760
If we go all the way back to episode one

00:41:47.760 --> 00:41:49.050
and bring up the lights a little,

00:41:49.050 --> 00:41:50.370
this is the same alcohol bottle

00:41:50.370 --> 00:41:52.170
that his brother Lucas was drinking from.

00:41:52.170 --> 00:41:53.490
I think the show does this to show

00:41:53.490 --> 00:41:55.470
that he too now has reached rock-bottom,

00:41:55.470 --> 00:41:57.840
just like his brother, and
neither one deals with this

00:41:57.840 --> 00:41:58.710
in a healthy way.

00:41:58.710 --> 00:42:00.780
Shortly after this, Junior meets Chucky.

00:42:00.780 --> 00:42:02.190
I would think that this would be proof

00:42:02.190 --> 00:42:04.680
that Lexy wasn't lying to
him back at the auditorium.

00:42:04.680 --> 00:42:06.870
Roll it.
(text swooshes)

00:42:06.870 --> 00:42:09.210
- Jake's doll Chucky was
alive and he killed his dad

00:42:09.210 --> 00:42:11.370
and he killed Oliver and
the cop at the hospital

00:42:11.370 --> 00:42:13.530
and your housekeeper too,
and he wouldn't stop killing

00:42:13.530 --> 00:42:15.210
so we broke him into
pieces and now he's dead.

00:42:15.210 --> 00:42:16.680
So everyone can stop worrying about it.

00:42:16.680 --> 00:42:18.780
- But, I don't know, maybe
since Junior didn't believe her,

00:42:18.780 --> 00:42:20.910
he just forgot or maybe
he just doesn't care

00:42:20.910 --> 00:42:22.080
because he's in a lot of pain

00:42:22.080 --> 00:42:24.030
and he's gonna become evil regardless.

00:42:24.030 --> 00:42:25.950
As I mentioned before,
the climax of the season

00:42:25.950 --> 00:42:27.780
revolves around this charity screening

00:42:27.780 --> 00:42:29.310
of James Whale's "Frankenstein".

00:42:29.310 --> 00:42:31.620
I see this as kind of the
completion of an analogy.

00:42:31.620 --> 00:42:32.490
In "Bride of Chucky",

00:42:32.490 --> 00:42:34.380
we saw Tiffany watching
"Bride of Frankenstein"

00:42:34.380 --> 00:42:36.000
so it's only natural that in "Chucky"

00:42:36.000 --> 00:42:37.680
she would be watching "Frankenstein".

00:42:37.680 --> 00:42:38.513
In the evening,

00:42:38.513 --> 00:42:40.830
Tiffany brings a prepared
meal by the house.

00:42:40.830 --> 00:42:43.740
- It's Swedish meatballs.

00:42:43.740 --> 00:42:44.777
- Which if you remember back to Bride,

00:42:44.777 --> 00:42:46.470
it was Chucky's favorite food.

00:42:46.470 --> 00:42:47.370
So it's very possible

00:42:47.370 --> 00:42:49.680
that she was actually bringing
this dish over for him,

00:42:49.680 --> 00:42:50.880
not for Junior's dad.

00:42:50.880 --> 00:42:52.890
I do wonder if she
obliged to do the dishes

00:42:52.890 --> 00:42:53.850
this time, though.

00:42:53.850 --> 00:42:55.770
Jake, who was attempting
to run away from home,

00:42:55.770 --> 00:42:57.300
finds himself in a chance encounter

00:42:57.300 --> 00:42:59.040
with an entirely new Good Guy doll

00:42:59.040 --> 00:43:00.840
and Logan would become
the victim of a kill

00:43:00.840 --> 00:43:02.888
that looks very familiar.

00:43:02.888 --> 00:43:05.212
(sinister music)

00:43:05.212 --> 00:43:07.900
(thunder rumbles)

00:43:07.900 --> 00:43:09.945
(sinister music)

00:43:09.945 --> 00:43:11.670
(thunder rumbles)

00:43:11.670 --> 00:43:14.310
- As Jake is trying to make
like a Fountains of Wayne lyric

00:43:14.310 --> 00:43:16.800
and get out of Hackensack,
he notices a delivery man

00:43:16.800 --> 00:43:20.130
carrying a Good Guy doll and
buys it off of him for $350.

00:43:20.130 --> 00:43:21.480
It must've been a pretty crappy job

00:43:21.480 --> 00:43:23.790
if he's willing to lose it for 350 bucks.

00:43:23.790 --> 00:43:24.840
This one is named Billy

00:43:24.840 --> 00:43:27.450
and appears not to be possessed
by Charles Lee Ray yet.

00:43:27.450 --> 00:43:29.790
The name Billy could be
an homage to Billy Boyd,

00:43:29.790 --> 00:43:32.100
the actor who voices
Glen in "Seed of Chucky"

00:43:32.100 --> 00:43:33.810
or perhaps it's another "Saw" reference.

00:43:33.810 --> 00:43:36.090
Billy the Puppet is one of
the only horror movie dolls

00:43:36.090 --> 00:43:38.230
who is as iconic as Chucky is.

00:43:38.230 --> 00:43:40.530
Or it could just be a random
name. In any event, we now know

00:43:40.530 --> 00:43:42.630
six of the 50 possible Good Guy names

00:43:42.630 --> 00:43:45.660
and I will not rest
until we know them all.

00:43:45.660 --> 00:43:47.070
With the knowledge of where this doll

00:43:47.070 --> 00:43:48.270
was supposed to be delivered,

00:43:48.270 --> 00:43:50.310
Jake returns to Hackensack
to save his friends

00:43:50.310 --> 00:43:51.570
from whatever is brewing.

00:43:51.570 --> 00:43:53.580
I'm comfortable referring
to Lexy and Devon

00:43:53.580 --> 00:43:54.810
as his friends at this point,

00:43:54.810 --> 00:43:57.600
but Lexy actually refers
to them as his family.

00:43:57.600 --> 00:43:58.590
- What family?

00:43:58.590 --> 00:44:01.860
- Me, Devon, the family you chose.

00:44:01.860 --> 00:44:03.600
- Which I get it, character development.

00:44:03.600 --> 00:44:04.590
Lexy has a heart now.

00:44:04.590 --> 00:44:06.390
She's doing the whole Dom Toretto meme.

00:44:06.390 --> 00:44:07.620
- [Dom] I got family.

00:44:07.620 --> 00:44:09.810
- But I still find it funny
that this is less than a month

00:44:09.810 --> 00:44:12.420
from her publicly making a
mockery of his dad's death

00:44:12.420 --> 00:44:14.250
and him trying to have her killed.

00:44:14.250 --> 00:44:16.080
Contrary to that, there's
also an interesting

00:44:16.080 --> 00:44:17.520
wardrobe choice in this scene.

00:44:17.520 --> 00:44:20.430
Before I noted how Lexy and
Junior wore matching hoodies.

00:44:20.430 --> 00:44:22.230
But as their relationship deteriorated,

00:44:22.230 --> 00:44:23.880
she no longer stayed in sync with him.

00:44:23.880 --> 00:44:25.350
Now she's matching with Jake.

00:44:25.350 --> 00:44:26.370
Hers is a different color,

00:44:26.370 --> 00:44:28.410
but they're both wearing
the same plaid pattern.

00:44:28.410 --> 00:44:30.420
I don't think this is
alluding to a relationship

00:44:30.420 --> 00:44:33.300
because Jake is stated
to be gay, not bisexual.

00:44:33.300 --> 00:44:34.170
But who knows?

00:44:34.170 --> 00:44:36.090
There is that line from
his father in episode one

00:44:36.090 --> 00:44:38.670
that suggests that Jake
doesn't know what he is yet.

00:44:38.670 --> 00:44:41.580
In any event, Jake is in time
to save his chosen family,

00:44:41.580 --> 00:44:44.190
but isn't quick enough to
save his actual family.

00:44:44.190 --> 00:44:45.300
In Logan's death scene,

00:44:45.300 --> 00:44:47.310
Chucky's head rotates around to greet him.

00:44:47.310 --> 00:44:49.380
This was originally a
reference to "The Exorcist",

00:44:49.380 --> 00:44:50.910
but it's since become a Chucky thing.

00:44:50.910 --> 00:44:53.520
It's happened in nearly every
entry since "Bride of Chucky".

00:44:53.520 --> 00:44:55.017
Junior is the one to
take his dad out, though.

00:44:55.017 --> 00:44:57.360
And he does it by beating him
down with the Chucky doll.

00:44:57.360 --> 00:44:58.740
The scene serves as a reminder

00:44:58.740 --> 00:45:00.060
of the ending of "Seed of Chucky",

00:45:00.060 --> 00:45:01.740
where Tiffany beats
her nanny over the head

00:45:01.740 --> 00:45:02.670
with the Tiffany doll.

00:45:02.670 --> 00:45:04.590
This doesn't seem to
hurt Chucky very much,

00:45:04.590 --> 00:45:07.200
which begs the question
of if Jake and Lexy's test

00:45:07.200 --> 00:45:09.210
to see if their dolls
were alive by beating them

00:45:09.210 --> 00:45:10.620
would've even done any good.

00:45:10.620 --> 00:45:12.690
It seems like fire is the
only thing painful enough

00:45:12.690 --> 00:45:13.590
to make him scream.

00:45:13.590 --> 00:45:16.560
In an attempt to rescue Devon,
Lexy calls them an Uber.

00:45:16.560 --> 00:45:18.270
- [Jake] Where's the Uber?

00:45:18.270 --> 00:45:19.170
- Four minutes.

00:45:19.170 --> 00:45:20.730
- I got kinda nervous when I heard that,

00:45:20.730 --> 00:45:22.710
but then I remembered that
Ubers are only dangerous

00:45:22.710 --> 00:45:23.580
in the reboot.

00:45:23.580 --> 00:45:25.620
After Chucky sees Junior
take out his father,

00:45:25.620 --> 00:45:27.990
we learned that this
was his goal all along.

00:45:27.990 --> 00:45:31.290
- You had no idea how hard
it's been getting one,

00:45:31.290 --> 00:45:35.520
you little sh*ts, to step
the **** up and play.

00:45:35.520 --> 00:45:37.980
- It seems like Chucky is
talking about his Super Bowl line

00:45:37.980 --> 00:45:39.870
way back in episode two.

00:45:39.870 --> 00:45:42.660
- It's the Super Bowl of slaughter.

00:45:42.660 --> 00:45:45.120
- This turns out to be the
final step of Chucky's ritual

00:45:45.120 --> 00:45:47.070
and the rest of his cult finally wakes up.

00:45:47.070 --> 00:45:49.200
But before he can rejoin
them in episode eight,

00:45:49.200 --> 00:45:50.370
An Affair to Dismember,

00:45:50.370 --> 00:45:53.310
which is a parody of the 1957
film "An Affair to Remember",

00:45:53.310 --> 00:45:55.020
Andy shows up at the Wheeler household

00:45:55.020 --> 00:45:56.190
to get in his rival's way.

00:45:56.190 --> 00:45:58.050
So Chucky just decides to hide.

00:45:58.050 --> 00:46:00.030
- He had a gun.

00:46:00.030 --> 00:46:01.230
I hate guns.

00:46:01.230 --> 00:46:06.230
They're like my Achilles'
heel along with axes, fire,

00:46:07.200 --> 00:46:11.340
and those big industrial size fans.

00:46:11.340 --> 00:46:14.430
- To quote the Chuck himself,
these are all actual examples.

00:46:14.430 --> 00:46:15.990
He was killed by an axe in Seed,

00:46:15.990 --> 00:46:17.610
he was thrown in the fireplace in one,

00:46:17.610 --> 00:46:20.490
and he was chopped up by a
big industrial fan in three,

00:46:20.490 --> 00:46:21.690
which, as you probably know,

00:46:21.690 --> 00:46:23.550
happens after most of
the movie takes place

00:46:23.550 --> 00:46:24.960
at Andy's military school.

00:46:24.960 --> 00:46:25.800
I find it interesting

00:46:25.800 --> 00:46:28.230
how Chucky has turned the
tables against Andy since then.

00:46:28.230 --> 00:46:29.610
Near the end of "Child's Play 3",

00:46:29.610 --> 00:46:31.380
Andy is essentially backed by an army

00:46:31.380 --> 00:46:32.640
and Chucky has to flee.

00:46:32.640 --> 00:46:34.830
Now, Chucky is the one
with an army behind him.

00:46:34.830 --> 00:46:37.260
There might even be a reference
to this in the dialogue.

00:46:37.260 --> 00:46:41.460
- We're gonna party like it's 1999.

00:46:41.460 --> 00:46:43.710
- According to my calculations
in the Chucky timeline video,

00:46:43.710 --> 00:46:46.410
1999 was the year that
"Child's Play 3" took place.

00:46:46.410 --> 00:46:48.240
So by saying this, he's essentially saying

00:46:48.240 --> 00:46:49.440
that they're going to kill Andy.

00:46:49.440 --> 00:46:52.340
The new recruits have a few
questions about the operation.

00:46:54.160 --> 00:46:58.890
- Is there an age limit
on potential victims?

00:46:58.890 --> 00:47:02.850
- Well, let's just say nobody
under the age of five or six.

00:47:02.850 --> 00:47:03.870
Fair enough?

00:47:03.870 --> 00:47:05.400
- Poor Andy was six years old

00:47:05.400 --> 00:47:06.540
in the original "Child's Play"

00:47:06.540 --> 00:47:08.310
so I guess he just missed the cutoff.

00:47:08.310 --> 00:47:10.290
As Tiffany brings down
some cookies to the party,

00:47:10.290 --> 00:47:12.660
we hear the song "Sick
Bubblegum" by Rob Zombie.

00:47:12.660 --> 00:47:14.610
I wanted to point this
out for two reasons.

00:47:14.610 --> 00:47:17.430
One, Rob Zombie also did
the song "Living Dead Girl"

00:47:17.430 --> 00:47:18.270
for "Bride of Chucky",

00:47:18.270 --> 00:47:20.160
which is essentially the
theme song of Tiffany.

00:47:20.160 --> 00:47:22.350
So it's fitting that she'd be
listening to some Rob Zombie

00:47:22.350 --> 00:47:23.310
in her own house.

00:47:23.310 --> 00:47:24.540
Two, earlier in this video,

00:47:24.540 --> 00:47:26.580
I talked about a whole lot
of "Halloween" references

00:47:26.580 --> 00:47:27.540
present in this season

00:47:27.540 --> 00:47:30.210
and Rob Zombie technically
is a "Halloween" director.

00:47:30.210 --> 00:47:32.040
It's not all fun and glam metal, though,

00:47:32.040 --> 00:47:33.420
as things would take a darker turn

00:47:33.420 --> 00:47:35.970
when Chucky orders Junior
to kill Nica under suspicion

00:47:35.970 --> 00:47:38.010
that Tiffany is developing
feelings towards her.

00:47:38.010 --> 00:47:39.690
The scene has an unexpected outcome

00:47:39.690 --> 00:47:41.430
when Tiffany turns and kills Chucky,

00:47:41.430 --> 00:47:43.830
or at least this particular
incarnation of Chucky.

00:47:43.830 --> 00:47:45.810
It calls back to that
flashback scene in the '80s

00:47:45.810 --> 00:47:47.940
when Charles Lee Ray and
Tiffany first hooked up

00:47:47.940 --> 00:47:49.410
and it looks like he's gonna kill Tiffany

00:47:49.410 --> 00:47:52.350
but then unexpectedly turns
and slashes up the other chick.

00:47:52.350 --> 00:47:53.640
So their relationship began

00:47:53.640 --> 00:47:55.200
with an unexpected change of allegiance,

00:47:55.200 --> 00:47:57.150
and now it's deteriorating with one.

00:47:57.150 --> 00:47:59.100
But then again, Chucky
and Tiffany's relationship

00:47:59.100 --> 00:48:00.690
has literally always been toxic

00:48:00.690 --> 00:48:02.610
so who knows if this
really means anything.

00:48:02.610 --> 00:48:04.920
We flashback to the '80s
again to see more of the night

00:48:04.920 --> 00:48:06.660
that Charles originally
transferred his soul

00:48:06.660 --> 00:48:07.710
out of his human body.

00:48:07.710 --> 00:48:10.050
After a fight, Tiffany can
be seen calling the police

00:48:10.050 --> 00:48:11.430
and she asked for Mike Norris,

00:48:11.430 --> 00:48:13.140
who, as we know from the original movie,

00:48:13.140 --> 00:48:15.510
is the one to kill Charles
Lee Ray at the toy store.

00:48:15.510 --> 00:48:18.240
So in a way, Chucky and
Tiffany were each responsible

00:48:18.240 --> 00:48:20.430
for killing each other's
original human form

00:48:20.430 --> 00:48:23.760
because nothing says love like
having your partner executed.

00:48:23.760 --> 00:48:25.020
I saw some people complaining

00:48:25.020 --> 00:48:27.480
that having Tiffany called
the cops on Chucky in 1988

00:48:27.480 --> 00:48:29.730
retcon's the flashback
from "Curse of Chucky".

00:48:29.730 --> 00:48:31.230
But if you actually watch that scene,

00:48:31.230 --> 00:48:33.510
the new information doesn't
actually change anything.

00:48:33.510 --> 00:48:36.360
Chucky accuses Sarah
Pierce of ratting him out.

00:48:36.360 --> 00:48:38.280
- You told him about us?

00:48:38.280 --> 00:48:40.980
- But she never actually
acknowledges that accusation.

00:48:42.630 --> 00:48:44.580
- There is no us.

00:48:44.580 --> 00:48:46.260
- Talking about the
character relationships

00:48:46.260 --> 00:48:48.150
really makes me wonder if Tiffany knows

00:48:48.150 --> 00:48:49.287
who Nica actually is.

00:48:49.287 --> 00:48:51.510
She obviously knows that she's
part of the Pierce family

00:48:51.510 --> 00:48:54.780
that Chucky brutalized in
2013, we see that much in Cult,

00:48:54.780 --> 00:48:55.830
but I don't know if she knows

00:48:55.830 --> 00:48:57.420
that Nica is the daughter of a woman

00:48:57.420 --> 00:48:59.130
that Chucky tried to have an affair with.

00:48:59.130 --> 00:49:01.620
It seems unlikely that
Tiffany would develop feelings

00:49:01.620 --> 00:49:03.300
for the daughter of her biggest rival

00:49:03.300 --> 00:49:04.470
for Charles's affection.

00:49:04.470 --> 00:49:05.910
Anyway, Andy Barclay gets there

00:49:05.910 --> 00:49:07.320
a little bit too late for the party,

00:49:07.320 --> 00:49:09.210
but he is at least in time to save Devon,

00:49:09.210 --> 00:49:10.590
who is still captive there.

00:49:10.590 --> 00:49:12.123
- Another goddamn head.

00:49:13.050 --> 00:49:13.980
Why not?

00:49:13.980 --> 00:49:15.450
- Of course this is a reference to Cult

00:49:15.450 --> 00:49:17.730
where Andy keeps the head of
a Chucky doll in captivity.

00:49:17.730 --> 00:49:20.070
This is just one of
many, many, many examples

00:49:20.070 --> 00:49:21.930
I've brought up throughout
this video of callbacks

00:49:21.930 --> 00:49:23.550
to the original seven Chucky movies.

00:49:23.550 --> 00:49:25.260
And I've already discussed
how the spotlight

00:49:25.260 --> 00:49:27.660
was more on "Child's
Play 2" than the others.

00:49:27.660 --> 00:49:29.790
What happens next is
another example of that.

00:49:29.790 --> 00:49:30.623
Only this time,

00:49:30.623 --> 00:49:33.437
these circumstances are
a little bit different.

00:49:33.437 --> 00:49:36.187
(sinister music)

00:49:38.430 --> 00:49:40.930
(tense music)

00:49:42.180 --> 00:49:44.040
After being abandoned at the gas station,

00:49:44.040 --> 00:49:46.320
Kyle still manages to
make her way to Hackensack

00:49:46.320 --> 00:49:48.200
where she protects Jake and
Lexy from the Chucky doll

00:49:48.200 --> 00:49:49.290
at Lexy's house.

00:49:49.290 --> 00:49:51.630
Then, for their own
safety, she drugs them.

00:49:51.630 --> 00:49:53.400
Yes, two kids that she's never met

00:49:53.400 --> 00:49:54.957
and she roofies them in
the first 10 minutes.

00:49:54.957 --> 00:49:57.007
And I love how she doesn't
even attempt to tell them,

00:49:57.007 --> 00:49:58.890
"Hey, you guys should just stay here.

00:49:58.890 --> 00:49:59.730
It's too dangerous.

00:49:59.730 --> 00:50:01.920
Don't worry, Andy and I are
gonna save your friend."

00:50:01.920 --> 00:50:03.960
No, she just goes straight to the roofies.

00:50:03.960 --> 00:50:05.400
Why is this her first idea?

00:50:05.400 --> 00:50:07.230
I mean, why does she
even have roofies on her

00:50:07.230 --> 00:50:08.580
when she gets locked out of the car?

00:50:08.580 --> 00:50:10.770
Not a good look, Kyle. Not a good look.

00:50:10.770 --> 00:50:12.960
She makes her way to the
Ray house on Sherwood Lane

00:50:12.960 --> 00:50:14.580
and unknowingly sets off the bomb,

00:50:14.580 --> 00:50:15.930
leaving Jake and Lexy to believe

00:50:15.930 --> 00:50:18.420
that her, Andy, and Devon
were inside during the blast.

00:50:18.420 --> 00:50:20.760
But they quickly learned
that Devon got out alive.

00:50:20.760 --> 00:50:22.950
The next day is the
Frankenstein Benefit Screening,

00:50:22.950 --> 00:50:25.740
where Tiffany, or as the public
knows her Jennifer Tilly,

00:50:25.740 --> 00:50:27.450
announces that these
Chucky dolls will be given

00:50:27.450 --> 00:50:29.700
to children in need, for some reason.

00:50:29.700 --> 00:50:31.590
Seeing the yellow boxes
stacked up like this

00:50:31.590 --> 00:50:32.820
should be a familiar sight

00:50:32.820 --> 00:50:34.650
to anyone who's seen "Child's Play 2".

00:50:34.650 --> 00:50:36.750
It's a reminder of the maze
of Good Guy doll products

00:50:36.750 --> 00:50:39.450
inside the Play Pals factory
at the conclusion of the film.

00:50:39.450 --> 00:50:41.340
This is an appropriate
time for this callback

00:50:41.340 --> 00:50:42.570
because what we're about to see

00:50:42.570 --> 00:50:44.670
would have history repeating itself.

00:50:44.670 --> 00:50:47.100
Lexy finds Junior in the back
hallway at the movie theater

00:50:47.100 --> 00:50:49.050
with Chucky riding on
his back at knifepoint

00:50:49.050 --> 00:50:50.160
and she gives chase.

00:50:50.160 --> 00:50:51.510
This is just like the scenario

00:50:51.510 --> 00:50:52.770
at the end of "Child's Play 2",

00:50:52.770 --> 00:50:54.750
where Andy was the one
being threatened by Chucky

00:50:54.750 --> 00:50:56.760
and Kyle was the blonde girl giving chase.

00:50:56.760 --> 00:50:58.440
Even the colors feel nostalgic here.

00:50:58.440 --> 00:51:00.690
The back section of the movie
theater is red and yellow,

00:51:00.690 --> 00:51:02.250
just like the maze at the factory.

00:51:02.250 --> 00:51:03.870
I probably don't need to point this out,

00:51:03.870 --> 00:51:05.130
but since we're past the point

00:51:05.130 --> 00:51:06.210
and we're lengthening this video

00:51:06.210 --> 00:51:07.380
a little bit matters at all,

00:51:07.380 --> 00:51:08.640
you may have noticed that what we see

00:51:08.640 --> 00:51:09.720
in the movie "Frankenstein"

00:51:09.720 --> 00:51:11.820
corresponds to what's
happening in our story.

00:51:11.820 --> 00:51:14.190
For example, we see Chucky
sitting next to Caroline,

00:51:14.190 --> 00:51:15.450
his new best friend to the end,

00:51:15.450 --> 00:51:16.770
and on screen we see the scene

00:51:16.770 --> 00:51:18.480
where the monster befriends a little girl.

00:51:18.480 --> 00:51:20.100
I'm not gonna point them all out because,

00:51:20.100 --> 00:51:21.780
again, I think this is pretty obvious.

00:51:21.780 --> 00:51:22.770
But if you didn't pick up on it,

00:51:22.770 --> 00:51:25.020
it's something that you can
look out for on your next watch.

00:51:25.020 --> 00:51:26.520
And I know I keep coming back to this,

00:51:26.520 --> 00:51:29.040
but once again it's the same
concept seen in "Scream"

00:51:29.040 --> 00:51:30.570
where the characters
are watching "Halloween"

00:51:30.570 --> 00:51:32.280
and it's intercut with similar scenarios

00:51:32.280 --> 00:51:33.450
going on in "Scream".

00:51:33.450 --> 00:51:36.360
By the way, Caroline is painted
to be a complete sociopath

00:51:36.360 --> 00:51:38.100
who continues to sit
there watching the movie

00:51:38.100 --> 00:51:40.020
even as everyone around
her is being killed

00:51:40.020 --> 00:51:42.690
and pays no mind to her dad who
has slumped over next to her

00:51:42.690 --> 00:51:44.430
as Jake and Devon tried
to get her out there.

00:51:44.430 --> 00:51:46.380
I think the creators
realized this in editing

00:51:46.380 --> 00:51:47.910
and tried to add this line.

00:51:47.910 --> 00:51:49.800
- [Caroline] But what about daddy?

00:51:49.800 --> 00:51:51.690
- You can just tell it
was dialogue replacement.

00:51:51.690 --> 00:51:53.970
By the way, Chucky's method
of murder in the movie theater

00:51:53.970 --> 00:51:56.400
is to hide underneath the
seats and stab up through them.

00:51:56.400 --> 00:51:57.420
It's the same thing he tried to do

00:51:57.420 --> 00:51:59.790
with Mike Norris's car seat in 1988.

00:51:59.790 --> 00:52:02.460
Behind the screen, Junior
describes how Chucky changed him

00:52:02.460 --> 00:52:03.660
and taught him to be a man.

00:52:03.660 --> 00:52:04.920
I noticed that he's wearing a hoodie

00:52:04.920 --> 00:52:07.020
similar to the one that
he had matching with Lexy,

00:52:07.020 --> 00:52:08.160
but this one is different.

00:52:08.160 --> 00:52:08.993
It's green.

00:52:08.993 --> 00:52:10.620
Junior is no longer the boy he was

00:52:10.620 --> 00:52:11.880
when he and Lexy split up.

00:52:11.880 --> 00:52:14.190
His short time with Chucky
has really changed him.

00:52:14.190 --> 00:52:16.230
Jake ends up in a physical altercation

00:52:16.230 --> 00:52:18.060
with his original Chucky
in the movie theater

00:52:18.060 --> 00:52:19.410
where Chucky's impressive strength,

00:52:19.410 --> 00:52:22.023
relative to his small
size, is finally explained.

00:52:23.910 --> 00:52:26.817
- You're nothing against the power,

00:52:26.817 --> 00:52:29.730
the great almighty Damballa.

00:52:29.730 --> 00:52:31.050
- Which is kind of different

00:52:31.050 --> 00:52:33.480
from how he pronounced the
great voodoo entity's name

00:52:33.480 --> 00:52:35.204
in the other movies.

00:52:35.204 --> 00:52:37.980
- Ade due Damballa.

00:52:37.980 --> 00:52:39.960
- But don't worry, it's not
like I made a whole video

00:52:39.960 --> 00:52:41.230
analyzing the history of Damballa

00:52:41.230 --> 00:52:43.432
where I took special care to pronounce it

00:52:43.432 --> 00:52:44.910
and how they pronounced it in the movies.

00:52:44.910 --> 00:52:49.140
- You dare defy the almighty Damballa?

00:52:49.140 --> 00:52:51.210
- Yeah, that doesn't bother me at all.

00:52:51.210 --> 00:52:53.280
Jake defeats Chucky using his bare hands,

00:52:53.280 --> 00:52:54.870
putting him in the same camp as Andy,

00:52:54.870 --> 00:52:56.490
who pulled Chucky apart with his own hands

00:52:56.490 --> 00:52:57.330
at the end of "Cult".

00:52:57.330 --> 00:52:58.470
I think this means that Jake

00:52:58.470 --> 00:53:00.270
is symbolically taking up the mantle

00:53:00.270 --> 00:53:02.820
as one of Chucky's greatest
rivals alongside Andy.

00:53:02.820 --> 00:53:04.680
It's something that we've
seen time and time again

00:53:04.680 --> 00:53:05.940
in this era of requels.

00:53:05.940 --> 00:53:08.190
The torch being passed to
the younger generation.

00:53:08.190 --> 00:53:10.080
We see similar moments in other movies.

00:53:10.080 --> 00:53:12.450
New characters taking the
reins from old characters.

00:53:12.450 --> 00:53:14.850
Luke Skywalker, Laurie Strode, Jigsaw,

00:53:14.850 --> 00:53:16.050
and Sidney Prescott.

00:53:16.050 --> 00:53:17.880
It seems like Jake gets
especially offended

00:53:17.880 --> 00:53:20.610
when Chucky calls his
relationship with Devon gay.

00:53:20.610 --> 00:53:23.550
- Oh, that is so gay.

00:53:23.550 --> 00:53:25.650
- Watch your f***in' mouth.

00:53:25.650 --> 00:53:27.330
That's my boyfriend you're talking about.

00:53:27.330 --> 00:53:28.590
- Can someone explain this to me?

00:53:28.590 --> 00:53:30.270
Like, is it still
considered to be offensive

00:53:30.270 --> 00:53:32.400
to be called gay if you're actually gay?

00:53:32.400 --> 00:53:34.290
'Cause if a gay person called me straight,

00:53:34.290 --> 00:53:35.917
I wouldn't be offended
and I'd just be like,

00:53:35.917 --> 00:53:37.110
"Yeah, accurate.

00:53:37.110 --> 00:53:38.190
Let me get your sister's number."

00:53:38.190 --> 00:53:39.660
Despite defeating this Chucky,

00:53:39.660 --> 00:53:41.130
there's still a whole truck of Chuck

00:53:41.130 --> 00:53:42.930
about to go out to the
children of America.

00:53:42.930 --> 00:53:44.310
This is a US→X truck,

00:53:44.310 --> 00:53:45.690
the same fictional shipping company

00:53:45.690 --> 00:53:48.150
that delivers all of the
dolls in the Curse-Seed arc.

00:53:48.150 --> 00:53:49.710
And Andy hijacks this truck.

00:53:49.710 --> 00:53:51.270
So he's no longer playing the victim.

00:53:51.270 --> 00:53:53.490
He's no longer the recipient
of Chucky's terror.

00:53:53.490 --> 00:53:55.200
He's now in the driver's seat.

00:53:55.200 --> 00:53:57.690
However, we forgot about one thing.

00:53:57.690 --> 00:53:59.880
Remember this Tiffany doll
that we saw momentarily

00:53:59.880 --> 00:54:00.780
at the end of "Cult"?

00:54:00.780 --> 00:54:02.790
So she's also gotten multiple incarnations

00:54:02.790 --> 00:54:03.840
running around at once.

00:54:03.840 --> 00:54:06.330
And just like in Bride where
she was first introduced,

00:54:06.330 --> 00:54:07.890
she's gonna be responsible for ensuring

00:54:07.890 --> 00:54:10.530
that the Chucky dolls reach
their intended destination.

00:54:10.530 --> 00:54:13.080
And she's gonna do so by
pointing a gun at the driver.

00:54:13.080 --> 00:54:15.330
As always, that was originally
from "Child's Play 2"

00:54:15.330 --> 00:54:17.010
where Chucky held Kyle at knifepoint

00:54:17.010 --> 00:54:18.360
and made her drive him around.

00:54:18.360 --> 00:54:19.290
Same situation.

00:54:19.290 --> 00:54:21.510
The male and female
characters are not swapped.

00:54:21.510 --> 00:54:23.040
The answer about what happens to Andy

00:54:23.040 --> 00:54:24.000
and the truckload of dolls

00:54:24.000 --> 00:54:25.500
is left as a cliffhanger this season.

00:54:25.500 --> 00:54:26.790
But we do see the next step

00:54:26.790 --> 00:54:28.500
in Tiffany and Nica's relationship.

00:54:28.500 --> 00:54:31.200
In order to prevent Chucky
from regaining control of Nica

00:54:31.200 --> 00:54:32.790
and potentially using it to attack her,

00:54:32.790 --> 00:54:35.280
Tiffany has amputated all of Nica's limbs.

00:54:35.280 --> 00:54:37.440
Obviously this has less
to do with practicality

00:54:37.440 --> 00:54:40.140
and more to do with Tiffany
being the most insane character.

00:54:40.140 --> 00:54:42.090
But it's hard to imagine that
Nica is gonna be able to do

00:54:42.090 --> 00:54:44.400
much of anything next
season in her current state.

00:54:44.400 --> 00:54:45.930
I'm guessing she'll be
transferring her soul

00:54:45.930 --> 00:54:48.330
into the body of a doll
or perhaps into the body

00:54:48.330 --> 00:54:51.030
of Hollywood actress
Fiona Dourif before long.

00:54:51.030 --> 00:54:54.060
And our season one comes
to a close in the cemetery,

00:54:54.060 --> 00:54:55.410
where Jake, Lexy, and Devon

00:54:55.410 --> 00:54:57.330
would visit the graves
of those that were lost.

00:54:57.330 --> 00:54:59.850
The season started with Jake
listening to Devon's podcast,

00:54:59.850 --> 00:55:01.710
Hackenslash and it would come full circle

00:55:01.710 --> 00:55:03.900
as we hear the latest
edition of that show.

00:55:03.900 --> 00:55:05.640
- [Devon] How do we stand
the chance against an enemy

00:55:05.640 --> 00:55:07.380
who disguises himself as our friend?

00:55:07.380 --> 00:55:08.280
- Back in "Child's Play",

00:55:08.280 --> 00:55:10.080
Chucky disguised himself
as a Good Guy doll

00:55:10.080 --> 00:55:11.910
and became Andy's best friend to the end.

00:55:11.910 --> 00:55:13.860
But now that phrase has
taken a new meaning.

00:55:13.860 --> 00:55:15.420
This time Chucky learned to manipulate

00:55:15.420 --> 00:55:16.800
their actual friend, Junior.

00:55:16.800 --> 00:55:18.870
I believe this is also the
first time in the entire show

00:55:18.870 --> 00:55:20.730
that Jake isn't wearing
that stupid necklace

00:55:20.730 --> 00:55:22.890
with the skull or doll
head or whatever it is.

00:55:22.890 --> 00:55:25.110
I think this represents
his change as a character.

00:55:25.110 --> 00:55:26.700
In the beginning, he doesn't have friends

00:55:26.700 --> 00:55:28.530
and he spent all of his
time collecting dolls

00:55:28.530 --> 00:55:29.640
and making art out of them.

00:55:29.640 --> 00:55:31.410
Now, he has real people in his life.

00:55:31.410 --> 00:55:33.480
At the very end, we see
that they're being watched

00:55:33.480 --> 00:55:35.670
and this person puts their
gloved hand on a tree,

00:55:35.670 --> 00:55:38.040
which is our only clue about
this person's identity.

00:55:38.040 --> 00:55:40.770
In episode seven, Kyle bought
two pairs of leather gloves

00:55:40.770 --> 00:55:42.750
for herself and Andy at
the gas station mart.

00:55:42.750 --> 00:55:43.830
Then in episode eight,

00:55:43.830 --> 00:55:46.260
there's an explosion at the
old Ray house on Sherwood Lane

00:55:46.260 --> 00:55:48.630
and we're led to believe that
those left inside perished,

00:55:48.630 --> 00:55:50.760
this includes Devon, Andy, and Kyle.

00:55:50.760 --> 00:55:52.920
We later find out that
Devon and Andy were okay,

00:55:52.920 --> 00:55:55.050
but according to this headline
in the Hackensack post

00:55:55.050 --> 00:55:57.420
there were fatalities
reported in the explosion.

00:55:57.420 --> 00:55:58.680
We're left to assume that that means

00:55:58.680 --> 00:56:00.180
that Kyle didn't make it.

00:56:00.180 --> 00:56:01.710
When Andy later hijacks the truck,

00:56:01.710 --> 00:56:04.410
we do see him wearing the
gloves but then he drives away,

00:56:04.410 --> 00:56:06.630
presumably still a hostage
of the Tiffany doll.

00:56:06.630 --> 00:56:08.670
This leads me to believe
that the hand on the tree

00:56:08.670 --> 00:56:09.780
is actually Kyle.

00:56:09.780 --> 00:56:11.550
And the fatality reported in the post

00:56:11.550 --> 00:56:12.990
was actually referring to the remains

00:56:12.990 --> 00:56:15.120
of the decapitated Chucky
left in the building.

00:56:15.120 --> 00:56:17.010
If the remaining pieces
were badly charred,

00:56:17.010 --> 00:56:18.840
police may have assumed
that this was a baby

00:56:18.840 --> 00:56:20.040
caught in the explosion.

00:56:20.040 --> 00:56:23.190
So I think this is Kyle, mostly
because it's hard to believe

00:56:23.190 --> 00:56:24.180
that they'd bring her back

00:56:24.180 --> 00:56:26.280
and then just have her
die off screen like that.

00:56:26.280 --> 00:56:28.590
While that may be the end of
the narrative for season one,

00:56:28.590 --> 00:56:31.200
we're not done, because I've
gotta talk about the epilogue.

00:56:31.200 --> 00:56:33.180
The scene features
Chucky lounging fireside

00:56:33.180 --> 00:56:34.590
and directly addressing the audience

00:56:34.590 --> 00:56:37.500
about the literary themes
explored in "Chucky" season one.

00:56:37.500 --> 00:56:39.870
This is yet another
parallel to "Frankenstein",

00:56:39.870 --> 00:56:41.730
more specifically "Bride of Frankenstein",

00:56:41.730 --> 00:56:43.890
which features a character
insert for Mary Shelley,

00:56:43.890 --> 00:56:44.940
the author of the novel,

00:56:44.940 --> 00:56:46.740
in an intro scene where she sits fireside

00:56:46.740 --> 00:56:48.150
and explains the moral of the story

00:56:48.150 --> 00:56:49.980
before the narrative actually starts.

00:56:49.980 --> 00:56:51.180
If you're a fan of my channel,

00:56:51.180 --> 00:56:53.010
you may remember me actually making a joke

00:56:53.010 --> 00:56:54.570
in my "'Bride of Chucky'
Things You Missed"

00:56:54.570 --> 00:56:56.880
about how they should have
done a similar fireside chat

00:56:56.880 --> 00:56:58.530
with Chucky creator Don Mancini.

00:56:58.530 --> 00:57:00.660
So I got a huge kick out
of this epilogue scene,

00:57:00.660 --> 00:57:02.130
especially this line.

00:57:02.130 --> 00:57:04.440
Roll it.
(text swooshes)

00:57:04.440 --> 00:57:08.490
- The eternal questions
explored by authors,

00:57:08.490 --> 00:57:13.490
such as Austin, Shakespeare, Mancini.

00:57:14.100 --> 00:57:15.810
- Kinda makes me wonder if Don Mancini

00:57:15.810 --> 00:57:17.610
has been watching a little CZsWorld.

00:57:17.610 --> 00:57:19.710
Kinda curious if he rang that death bell.

00:57:19.710 --> 00:57:21.330
But one horror movie analysis channel

00:57:21.330 --> 00:57:23.100
that he's almost definitely been watching

00:57:23.100 --> 00:57:24.390
is our friend Dead Meat,

00:57:24.390 --> 00:57:26.340
who is most known for
his world's famous show

00:57:26.340 --> 00:57:28.050
the Kill Count, where
he counts up the kills

00:57:28.050 --> 00:57:29.057
in all your favorite horror movies,

00:57:29.057 --> 00:57:31.770
'cause that's exactly
what Chucky does here.

00:57:31.770 --> 00:57:36.750
- And speaking of who died,
let's review, shall we?

00:57:36.750 --> 00:57:39.210
- We also saw Chucky embrace
the idea of a kill count

00:57:39.210 --> 00:57:41.220
during his last confrontation with Jake.

00:57:41.220 --> 00:57:43.620
- [Chucky] Eventually they're
gonna forget the names

00:57:43.620 --> 00:57:46.650
of everybody who died here tonight.

00:57:46.650 --> 00:57:51.120
All they'll remember is the
number of people I killed,

00:57:51.120 --> 00:57:52.590
my body count.

00:57:52.590 --> 00:57:54.150
- This is something that
we've been seeing more

00:57:54.150 --> 00:57:56.580
in the horror genre, the idea
of a built-in kill count.

00:57:56.580 --> 00:57:57.570
We saw it in "Us"

00:57:57.570 --> 00:57:59.310
and we see it getting
much more attention here

00:57:59.310 --> 00:58:01.350
as a full-blown segment
at the end of the season.

00:58:01.350 --> 00:58:03.180
I think the challenge
is on for season two,

00:58:03.180 --> 00:58:05.010
not only to surpass the 21 kills

00:58:05.010 --> 00:58:06.300
racked up over the first season,

00:58:06.300 --> 00:58:08.490
but to also break the
record that it just set

00:58:08.490 --> 00:58:10.050
for most things you missed.

00:58:10.050 --> 00:58:11.910
To find out if season two pulls it off,

00:58:11.910 --> 00:58:13.830
make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld

00:58:13.830 --> 00:58:15.150
for new horrors every week.

00:58:15.150 --> 00:58:17.490
Ring the death bell and
select all notifications

00:58:17.490 --> 00:58:20.010
and I will see you in the next season.

00:58:20.010 --> 00:58:22.350
Assuming we both survive.

00:58:22.350 --> 00:58:24.570
Now, can anyone remember
the name of the doll

00:58:24.570 --> 00:58:25.770
that this show is about?

00:58:26.605 --> 00:58:30.105
(upbeat electronic music)

